Perfect For Gimbal Monitoring. This cable is the thinnest BNC cable we offer and works great on gimbals. Being that thin also makes it more susceptible to kinking and other damage. If you’d like a tougher cable we offer this Belden 3ft cable.

Ultra-Miniature Coax Cable. The Belden 2.6ft Ultra Thin 3G-SDI BNC Cable is TINY. It’s hard to overstate how lightweight the 2.46mm diameter ultra-miniature coax cable is. This listing is for our 2.6 foot version of the cable that is perfectly suited for video monitoring on three-axis gimbals and other applications where weight reduction is of the utmost importance.

Neutrik Rear TWIST Connectors. Neutrik makes great connectors in general, but this design ups the ante. Inferior BNC connectors twist at the metal BNC coupler and can be difficult to detach in tight quarters. This rear twist connector can be turned at the boot, and it’s hard to go back. This 2.6ft cable features a black boot to help distinguish it from our other lengths of SDI cables. We include an angled BNC adapter to help with awkward SDI port placement.

3 GHz Signal Transmission. This Belden SDI cable is 1080p-ready and rated for 3G transmission.

Updated Cables Available. We now carry the Belden 2.6ft 179DT 12G-SDI BNC Cable, which is backwards compatible with 6G and 3G applications.

