INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (508, 1, 32, 'Blackmagic Design PYXIS 6K (EF)', 'blackmagic-design-pyxis-6k-ef', 'The Blackmagic Design PYXIS 6K (EF) is a high-end, next-generation cinema system designed for maximum compatibility. Key features include:

Full-frame 6K sensor with 6:5 anamorphic
13-stop dynamic range and ISO up to 25,600
Built-in live streaming support
In-body touchscreen HDR monitor

Exceptional Low-Light Performance. Featuring dual-native ISO at 400/3200 with a range extending up to 25,600, the PYXIS is equipped to handle nearly any shooting environment. This is further supported by a wide 13-stop dynamic range, rich color, and accurate skin tones. Special note: this camera lacks built-in ND filters.

Format Flexibility. The Blackmagic Design PYXIS is benefitted by a large full-frame sensor that allows you to work in a variety of film formats and aspect ratios, from open gate 3:2 to 6:5 anamorphic to Super 35. Shoot up to 36 fps using the full area of the sensor, 60 fps in anamorphic, or 120 fps in Super 16. Please note that this camera does not have a global shutter. It is equipped with a rolling shutter. Recording is done only in Blackmagic RAW (with H.264 for proxies) to Blackmagic Cloud, CFexpress Type B cards, external flash disks, or SSDs. For a version of this camera that can do open gate 12K, check out the PYXIS 12K for EF mount.

Fully Riggable Camera for Any Set. Blackmagic designed the PYXIS 6K with the ambition of creating the world’s most riggable full-frame cinema camera. It has multiple mounting points all over the body and two convenient mounting plates: a standard plate for attaching mics and accessories and an SSD plate for attaching a drive or your phone. The Rosette Plate for PYXIS 6K is available separately. The in-body HDR touchscreen eliminates the need for an extra monitor (though there are mounting ports for attaching an optional monitor). It offers access to all the settings, focus assist, the ability to display LUTs, and a wide range of other helpful screen overlays. Settings can also be accessed via physical buttons so that you aren’t reliant on the screen for changing important functions.

Streaming Support. Stream in 1080p directly from the PYXIS via Secure Reliable Transport (SRT) and Real Time Messaging Protocol (RTMP) for stable, low-latency communication with YouTube, Facebook, and many other social platforms. Connect to Ethernet or use your 4G/5G phone for mobile data. Observe your streaming status directly on the LCD or pair this camera with the optional Blackmagic ATEM Streaming Bridge to create a wireless link back to the studio for your crew to keep up with live performances, corporate talks, and so much more.

Expansive Connectivity. The form factor of the Blackmagic Design PYXIS lends itself to a large offering of connections. It has two CFexpress Type B card slots (supports relay style continuous recording on the second slot, not dual-footage recording), 12G-SDI out, a front USB-C port (for an optional viewfinder), a back USB-C port (for external recording devices or a phone), Timecode, Ethernet, headphone jack, and a mini-XLR port with +48V phantom power for a microphone as well as a 3.5mm option. There are also built-in microphones with an extremely low noise floor and built-in speakers for quick playback review.

Lens Compatibility and Power. Both full-frame and APS-C/crop-frame EF-mount lenses can be paired with this camera thanks to its plethora of shooting formats, as well as anamorphic lenses. Power the camera with the included 12V DC power cable or with BP-U series batteries, which are available separately. A BP-U100 will get you about 3 hours of runtime.', 700000.0, '{"Brand":"Blackmagic","Camera Mount":"Canon EF","Camera Type":"Cinema","Compatible Media":"CFexpress Type B","General":"Accessory Mounts9x 1/4\\"-203x 3/8\\"-164x M4No shoe mountBattery TypeBP-U seriesDimensions (W x H x D)4.17 × 4.69 × 5.94″Mfr. Model Number CINECAMCPYXD60LFEFMonitorEVF not included (available here)4\\" fixed touchscreenWeight3.3 lb.WirelessBluetooth","Imaging":"ISODynamic Range: 13 stopsISO Range: Dual gain 400/3,200 (25,600 expanded)Max Resolution6K (6048 × 4032)ND FiltersNoSensor24.6MP Full Frame CMOSShutterElectronic rollingStabilizationNo","Inputs/Outputs":"Audio I/O1x 3.5mm headphone jack1x 3.5mm mic jack1x 3-pin mini-XLR mic/line (+48V phantom power)Other I/O1x USB-C (data)1x BNC (ref/TC)1x EthernetPower I/O1x 2-pin LEMO (12V DC)1x BP-U battery portStorage I/O2x CFexpress Type B slots1x SSD with URSA Mini Recorder (not included)Video I/O1x BNC (12G-SDI)","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Video Resolution":"6K","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Fixed","Sensor Size":"Full-Frame","Stabilization":"No","Video Capture":"Shooting Resolutions, Blackmagic RAW6048 × 4032 (Open Gate 3:2) up to 36 fps4832 × 4032 (Anamorphic 6:5) up to 36 fps6048 × 3408 (6K 16:9) up to 46 fps6048 × 3200 (6K DCI 17:9) up to 48 fps6048 × 2520 (6K 2.4:1) up to 60 fps4096 × 3072 (Super 35 4:3) up to 50 fps4096 × 2304 (4K 16:9) up to 60 fps4096 × 2160 (4K DCI 17:9) up to 60 fps2112 × 1184 (Super 16 16:9) up to 100 fps1920 × 1080 (1080 HD 16:9) up to 120 fps","Weather Sealing":"No","Wireless Connectivity":"Bluetooth"}', 'Blackmagic
