Format Friendly. The URSA Cine’s large-format sensor creates a flexible environment for aspect ratios, lenses, and delivery formats. With a stunning 3:2 open gate image, you can easily reframe your shots in post-production. There’s plenty of benefits to this redesigned sensor, including the ability to shoot in 4K, 8K, or 12K using the entire sensor without cropping and retaining the full field-of-view. You can even shoot with classic cinema lenses using one of the three available 9K Super 35 modes!

Monitoring and Camera Control. To monitor your productions, the URSA Cine sports a fold-out monitor with a 5-inch touchscreen on one side and an external color status LCD on the other. With the dedicated assist station located on the right-side of the camera, you have access to another 5-inch HDR touchscreen that helps prevent the need for external monitors.

Inputs and Outputs. To meet the demands of high-end productions, the URSA Cine is packed out with connections all around. You’re provided with 7-pin LEMO and 3-pin Fischer connectors for record start/stop, a standard 24V 8-pin LEMO connector for camera power, and an additional 2-pin LEMO 12V connection to power lower-voltage accessories. For external monitoring, you have access to two 12G-SDI outputs, plus a 10G Ethernet connection for syncing to Blackmagic Cloud media.

Built-In Filters. For those moments you’re in need of light reduction and minimized interference, this camera has built-in OLPF and ND filters. The integrated OLPF is precisely matched to that stellar sensor we’ve chatted about, and is designed to minimize the interference that comes along with shooting materials and fabrics. The three integrated ND filters are available to you in reductions of 2-, 4- and 6-stops. Even in the harshest of lighting, these filters can save the day of production.

Internal Recording Available. This URSA Cine is the first digital film camera that comes equipped with the ultra-fast Blackmagic Media Module to internally store up to 8TB of footage! This storage solution allows you to record at the highest resolutions and frame rates for hours, and even access your files over 10G Ethernet. If you’re using several URSA Cine cameras with the modules, you can add up to three of them to the separately available Blackmagic Design Media Dock to gain access to more files at once, speeding up post-production and turnaround times.

Wireless Capabilities and Streaming. Like most cameras of this generation, the URSA Cine is capable of WiFi and 10G Ethernet connections. With a built-in hardware engine that supports RTMP and SRT streaming, the URSA Cine can stream directly to clients or major streaming platforms. While live streaming, you can use the USB-C port to connect an Apple or Android device to gain internet connection!

