Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (674, 2, 49, 'Canon 100mm f/2.8L IS Macro', 'canon-100mm-f-2-8l-is-macro', 'The Canon 100mm f/2.8L IS Macro is a major improvement over the excellent Canon 100mm f/2.8 Macro it replaces. Key features include:

Four-stop image stabilization
Weather sealed
Improved motor
Improved aperture ring

Improved Image Stabilization. The Canon 100mm f/2.8L IS Macro boasts L-series designation, weather sealing, and Canon’s four-stop hybrid image-stabilization system. The hybrid image-stabilization system compensates for linear and rotational shake, making image stabilization more effective at close distances.

Advanced Optics and Focusing. With fifteen elements in twelve groups, an improved ultrasonic motor, and a nine-blade aperture ring for smooth out-of-focus highlights, the f/2.8L IS Macro represents a major improvement over the already-excellent lens it replaces.', 221000.0, '{"Angle of View":"24°","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.06 × 4.84″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"67mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"100-100","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"12/15","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Macro and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"2.8","Maximum Magnification":"1x","Mfr. Model Number":"3554B002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"11.81\\"","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.4lb","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', '100mm f/2.8L
IS
Macro
Front & rear caps
ET-73 hood
	67mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (675, 2, 49, 'Canon 11-24mm f/4L', 'canon-11-24mm-f-4l', 'The Canon 11-24mm f/4L is a high-quality ultra-wide angle zoom that’s optimized for full-frame Canon DSLRs. Key features include:

Premium image quality
Ultra-wide 11mm zoom with 126° of coverage
35mm full-frame coverage
Near-silent ultrasonic motor

Ultra-Wide Zoom. With 126° of coverage at 11mm, the 11-24mm f/4L is Canon’s widest rectilinear zoom lens.  This ultra-wide’s extremely high image quality with minimal distortion makes it a perfect choice for landscape and architectural photography.  It covers the ultra-wide to moderately wide focal lengths and has constant f/4 aperture throughout the zoom range.

Full-Frame Coverage. The ultra-wide angle zoom offers 35mm full-frame coverage, making it compatible with Canon’s full line of EF-mount DSLRs.  When mounted to a crop-frame APS-C camera, it offers a 17.6-38.4mm equivalent focal length.

Ultrasonic Motor. This internal focusing lens utilizes a ring-type Ultrasonic Motor (USM) for fast, near-silent performance for both still and video use.  It’s full-time manual for quick tweaks on the go, and the dedicated AF/MF switch allows you to disengage autofocus entirely when desired.

L-Series Quality. As part of the L-series, image and build quality are premium.  The 11-24mm f/4L does not disappoint.  It features four aspheric, one ultra low-dispersion, and one “super” ultra low-dispersion lens elements that effectively correct barrel distortion while reducing chromatic aberrations from corner to corner throughout the zoom range.  It has fluorine coatings on external elements and subwavelength coatings on the internal elements to minimize image quality-robbing flare and ghosting.  The weather-sealed lens barrel provides protection from the elements, with the fluorine coatings doing double-time by repelling dust and fingerprints.

Built-In Hood. Do note that the lens hood is built into the lens barrel, so there’s no taking it off.  This also means there’s no threaded filter ring.  However, the lens does accept rear gel filters.', 468000.0, '{"Angle of View":"126°-84° 5’","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"4.25 × 5.2″ (ø x L)","Filter Type":"Rear Mount","Focal Length":"11-24","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"11/16","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"4","Maximum Magnification":"0.16x","Mfr. Model Number":"9520B002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"11.02\\"","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"2.6lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', 'Canon 11-24mm
Front & rear caps
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (676, 4, 49, 'Canon 12-Pin to 12-Pin Interface Extension Cable 15.7-inch', 'canon-12-pin-to-12-pin-interface-extension-cable-15-7-inch', 'Extend your servo controller from your ENG broadcast lens when it is mounted on a Canon EOS C500 Mark II or C300 Mark III cinema camera with this 12-Pin to 12-Pin Servo Extension Cable from Canon.

The Canon 12-Pin to 12-Pin Interface Extension Cable is essential for extending servo control from ENG broadcast lenses and select Canon camcorders. This extension cable allows for camera controlled servo with broadcast lenses like the Canon Cine Servo 25-250mm T2.9 or 17-120mm T2.9-3.9 with the Canon EOS C300 MK III or C500 MK II when paired with the EU-V2. It is also compatible with external controllers like the Canon ZSD-300D or FPD-400D. This version measures 15.7" in length.', 79000.0, '{"Brand":"Canon","Cable Type":"Power, Control, Accessory, and Extender","Connector":"Unknown","Item Type":"Cable","Length":"1.4’","Mfr. Model Number":"0149T313"}', 'Just the cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (677, 4, 49, 'Canon 12-Pin to 12-Pin Interface Extension Cable 7.9-inch', 'canon-12-pin-to-12-pin-interface-extension-cable-7-9-inch', 'The Canon 12-Pin to 12-Pin Interface Extension Cable is essential for extending servo control from ENG broadcast lenses and select Canon camcorders. This extension cable allows for camera controlled servo with broadcast lenses like the Canon Cine Servo 25-250mm T2.9 or 17-120mm T2.9-3.9 with the Canon EOS C300 MK III or C500 MK II when paired with the EU-V2. It is also compatible with external controllers like the Canon ZSD-300D or FPD-400D. This version measures 7.9" in length.', 79000.0, '{"Brand":"Canon","Cable Type":"Power and Control","Connector":"Unknown","Item Type":"Cable","Length":"0.6’","Mfr. Model Number":"0149T722"}', 'Just the cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (678, 2, 49, 'Canon 135mm f/2L', 'canon-135mm-f-2l', 'The Canon 135mm f/2L is a very sharp, fast lens that’s great on full-frame and crop-frame cameras alike. Key features include:

Fantastic long portrait lens
L-series build quality
Great value

Very Sharp and Fast. A popular Canon L-series prime, the Canon 135mm f/2L is a very sharp, very fast lens that’s wonderful for long-portrait and “head-and-shoulder” shooting on full-frame cameras. On crop frame cameras, it’s a great short telephoto or long-portrait lens.

Narrow Depth of Field. The f/2 maximum aperture provides narrow depth of field, produces great bokeh, and allows clean shots even in dim light.', 254000.0, '{"Angle of View":"18°","Aperture Blades":"8, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.25 × 4.41″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"72mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"135-135","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"8/10","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Telephoto and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"2","Maximum Magnification":"0.2x","Mfr. Model Number":"2520A004","Minimum Focusing Distance":"2.95’","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.65lb","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Canon 135mm
Front & rear caps
ET-78II hood
	72mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (679, 2, 49, 'Canon 14mm f/2.8L II', 'canon-14mm-f-2-8l-ii', 'The Canon 14mm f/2.8L II is an ultra-wide angle rectilinear lens that’s ideal for architectural photography. Key features include:

Completely redesigned optics
114° field of view
L-series build quality
Perfect for architectural work

High-Quality Redesigned Optics. The Canon 14mm f/2.8L II is an ultra-wide angle rectilinear lens has completely redesigned optics and is extremely sharp without much chromatic aberration. With a 114° field of view and low distortion, this lens is ideal for architectural photography.', 371000.0, '{"Angle of View":"114°","Aperture Blades":"6, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.15 × 3.7″ (ø x L)","Filter Type":"Rear Mount","Focal Length":"14-14","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"2.8","Maximum Magnification":"0.15x","Mfr. Model Number":"2045B002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"7.87\\"","Optical Design":"14/11","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.4lb","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', '14mm f/2.8L
II
Front & rear caps
Built-in hood
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (680, 2, 49, 'Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L II', 'canon-16-35mm-f-2-8l-ii', 'The Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L II is a very good wide-angle, f/2.8 zoom. Looking for an updated version of this lens? Check out the 16-35mm f/2.8L III. Key features include:

Great all-around wide angle zoom
L-series build quality
Excellent value

Solid Wide-Angle Zoom. The Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L II is reasonably sharp at the edges and corners, and is relatively flare resistant. There’s a little distortion at extreme wide-angle shots, but nothing that isn’t easily corrected in post. That said, if you don’t need the f/2.8 aperture, the Canon 17-40 lens is its equal in resolution, perhaps a bit more flare resistant, and far less expensive.', 339000.0, '{"Angle of View":"108° 10’-63°","Aperture Blades":"7","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.48 × 4.39″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"82mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"16-35","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"12/16","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle and Wide Angle","Maximum Aperture":"2.8","Maximum Magnification":"0.22x","Mfr. Model Number":"1910B002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"0.9’","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.4lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', '16-35mm f/2.8L
II
Front & rear caps
EW-88
Hood
	82mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (681, 2, 49, 'Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L III', 'canon-16-35mm-f-2-8l-iii', 'The Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L III is Canon’s flagship wide-angle zoom lens for full-frame Canon EF-mount cameras, and an update to the popular Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L II. Key features include:

Great for landscape and event photography
Fast, nearly silent autofocus
Redesigned optical formula
Improved build quality

What’s New. The redesigned optical formula promises greatly improved performance in a durable, weather-resistant body, relative to its predecessor, the Canon 16-35mm f/2.8L II.

Fast and Wide. Optimized for full-frame cameras, the 16-35L III offers users ultra-wide to moderately wide zoom-range coverage with a fast f/2.8 constant aperture. Its excellent angle of view and light-gathering ability make it a favorite among landscape and event photographers.

Ultrasonic Focusing Motor. This lens uses a ring-type Ultrasonic Motor to provide fast, nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters.

Improved Optics. Its predecessor left a bit to be desired in corner performance. For this new generation, Canon redesigned the optical formula to address the issue head-on. Using a combination of two large-diameter GMO dual-surface aspherical elements, one ground aspherical element, and two UD elements, the 16-35mm f/2.8L III boasts edge-to-edge sharpness throughout the zoom range with minimal distortion, chromatic aberrations, and color blurring.

High-Quality Build. With each generation, we expect to see improved build quality. This third-gen 16-35 follows suit, bringing fluorine coatings to the front and rear elements to resist dust, fingerprints, and smudging. Additionally, the weather sealing has been improved to help keep mother nature on the outside.', 357000.0, '{"Angle of View":"108° 10’ to 63°","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.48 × 5.02″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"82mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"16-35","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"11/16","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"2.8","Maximum Magnification":"0.22x","Mfr. Model Number":"0573C002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"11.02\\"","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.74lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', '16-35mm
III lens
Front & rear caps
EW-88D hood
	82mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (682, 2, 49, 'Canon 16-35mm f/4L IS', 'canon-16-35mm-f-4l-is', 'The Canon 16-35mm f/4L IS is a high-quality wide-angle zoom that’s optimized for full-frame Canon DSLRs. Key features include:

Premium image quality
4-stop image stabilization
108° coverage
Optimized for full-frame DSLRs

Ultra-Wide Zoom. Offering 108° of coverage at its widest, the 16-35mm f/4L IS is great choice for landscape, street, and event photography. It covers the ultra-wide to moderately wide focal lengths and has constant f/4 aperture throughout the zoom range.

Image Stabilization. Provides up to 4 stops of correction, enabling you to shoot static subjects at slower shutter speeds without fear of blur.

Full-Frame Coverage. The ultra-wide angle zoom offers 35mm full-frame coverage, making it compatible with Canon’s full line of EF-mount DSLRs.

L-Series Quality. As an L-series lens, image and build quality are premium. It features three aspheric lens elements to correct aberrations, two UD elements help reduce chromatic aberrations from corner to corner throughout the zoom range, and fluorine coatings to repel dust and minimize ghosting. The ring-type USM motor provides fast, silent performance with full-time manual override. Internal focusing ensures the physical size of the lens doesn’t change while focusing, and the weather-sealed barrel provides protection from the elements.', 221000.0, '{"Angle of View":"108°-63° 10’","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.25 × 4.44″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"77mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"16-35","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"12/16","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"4","Maximum Magnification":"0.23x","Mfr. Model Number":"9518B002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"11.02\\"","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.35lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', '16-35mm f/4L
IS
Front & rear caps
EW-82 hood
B+W 77mm filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (683, 2, 49, 'Canon 17-40mm f/4L', 'canon-17-40mm-f-4l', 'The Canon 17-40mm f/4L is an excellent wide-angle lens at a very reasonable price. It’s great for close-up work. Key features include:

L-series build quality
11-inch minimum focusing distance
Near-silent ultrasonic motor
Great value

Excellent for Close-Up Work. The lens’s minimum focusing distance is just 11 inches (28cm) throughout its entire range of focal lengths, which makes it very useful for close-up work. All of the focusing and zooming action is done internally, with no changes in the lens’s size.

Sharp Image Quality. It’s a stop slower than the Canon 16-35 f/4L IS5, but otherwise there’s very little difference between them. Some reviewers have found the 17-40 is actually sharper at the wide end, and it may be less prone to lens flare.', 139000.0, '{"Angle of View":"104°-57° 30’","Aperture Blades":"7, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"3.29 × 3.81″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"77mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On and Rear Mount","Focal Length":"17-40","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"9/12","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"4","Maximum Magnification":"0.24x","Mfr. Model Number":"8806A002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"11.02\\"","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.1lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', '17-40mm f/4L
Front & rear caps
EW-83E hood
	77mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (684, 1, 49, 'Canon 1DX Mark II', 'canon-1dx-mark-ii', 'The 1DX Mark II is Canon’s flagship DSLR and an upgrade to the original 1DX and the predecessor to the Canon 1DX Mark III. Key features include:

20.2MP CMOS sensor
Improved dual-pixel autofocus with 41 cross-type points
Up to 16 fps continuous shooting
Enhanced ISO performance

Mark II Fever. The Mark II is more about refinement than knock-your-socks-off features. Seeing as its target market is professional photographers, Canon has prioritized reliability over fancy features that may or may not work. With that said, the Mark II surpasses its predecessor in many ways: it boasts a higher-resolution full-frame sensor with improved, dual-pixel autofocus; a faster continuous frame rate; built-in GPS; and in-camera 4K capture. If this still isn’t enough for your shoot, check out the updated Canon 1DX Mark III.

20.2MP Full-Frame CMOS Sensor. The modest increase in MP isn’t going to be noticeable to most, but the increase in performance that comes along with the higher-resolution sensor definitely will. Dual DIGIC 6+ processors help the new sensor to offer improved high performance throughout its normal ISO 100-51,200 range (expandable to 50-409,600), 14 fps (continuous focus)/16 fps (locked focus/exposure, live view), and generous unlimited-JPG/170-RAW buffer.

Improved AF. It’s not an entirely new autofocus system, but rather an overhauled version of its predecessors. What you get is a 61-point system (all user-selectable—no trickery) with 41 cross-type points. The difference comes in all 61 points supporting f/8 autofocus, the 360,000-pixel RGB+IR metering sensor for better exposure and tracking performance, and wider-spaced points for slightly larger frame coverage.

Dual-Pixel AF. The Mark II is the first full-frame sensor with Canon’s dual-pixel AF system. Limited to video shooting, this system uses phase-detection for continuous autofocus and tracking with user-adjustable sensitivity and speed settings. The camera also offers rack focusing via the touchscreen rear LCD when shooting video.

4K Video. While it’s not quite as feature-rich as the 1DC, the Mark II captures DCI 4K up to 60p (4:2:2/8-bit) and Full HD up to 120p (4:2:0/8-bit). 4K capture is limited to a central 1.3x crop of the sensor, while Full HD utilizes the full sensor frame. Clean HDMI output tops out at 1080p for external recording. Audio is handled by the in-camera stereo mic or externally using the 3.5mm input, with real-time monitoring possible thanks to the 3.5mm headphone jack. Please note that there’s no focus peaking or zebra warnings, so we recommend an external electronic viewfinder/video monitor with those features.

Professional Build. Just as you’d expect from a 1D-series camera, the Mark II is built like a tank. The magnesium-alloy body features built-in vertical grip, dust- and weather-sealing, multiple customizable buttons, bright 0.76x optical pentaprism with 100% viewfinder coverage, and a 3.2-inch, 1.62m-dot rear LCD with limited touch-sensitivity (video AF point selection only). The new higher-capacity LP-E19 battery offers up to 1210 shots per charge, but the Mark II offers backwards compatibility with the previous LP-E4N battery, albeit with a reduced top continuous shooting rate of 14 fps.

Dual CFast 2.0/CF Memory. To keep up with the increase in data flow, the Mark II takes advantage of the CFast 2.0 format. While Canon made the second slot CompactFlash, if you’re looking to get the most out of the Mark II, you’ll need to use CFast cards. 4K video recording for up to 30 minutes and 170-shot RAW buffer are based on using CFast. Try to use even the fastest of CF cards and that drops to a couple minutes of 4K video and a 73-shot RAW buffer. Long story short, use CFast as your primary card and CF as backup.', 818000.0, '{"Brand":"Canon","Camera Mount":"Canon EF","Camera Type":"DSLR","Compatible Media":"CF and CFast","Flash":"Type \\t\\tExternal Only Maximum Sync Speed \\t\\t1/250 Second \\tFlash Compensation \\t\\t-3 EV to +3 EV (in 1/3 or 1/2 EV steps) \\tFlash System \\t\\tDedicated: eTTL \\t\\tConnection: Hot Shoe/PC Terminal","Imaging":"Maximum Resolution \\t\\tEffective Pixels: Approximately 20.2 MP \\t\\t3 × 2: 5472 × 3648 16 × 9: 4096 × 2160 \\tSensor \\t\\tType: CMOS 35mm \\t\\tSize: 36 × 24mm \\tCrop Factor \\t\\tx1.0 \\tBit Depth \\t\\tPhoto: 14-bit HD Video: 4:2:0 8-bit 4K Video: 4:2:2 8-bit \\tISO \\t\\tDynamic Range: Approximately 13.5 Stops \\t\\tDefault Sensitivity Range: 100-51,200 \\t\\tExpanded Sensitivity Range: 50-409,600 \\t\\tNative ISO: 100","Inputs/Outputs":"Audio Inputs \\t\\tMic: 3.5 mm (⅛”) stereo mini-jack \\tAudio Output \\t\\tHeadphones: 3.5 mm (⅛”) stereo mini-jack \\tVideo Outputs \\t\\tHDMI Type C (mini-HDMI) \\tAdditional Inputs/Outputs \\t\\tRemote: Canon N3-Type","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Photo Resolution":"21.5 MP","Maximum Video Resolution":"4K","Mfr. Model Number":"0931C002","Monitoring":"Viewfinder \\t\\tType: Pentaprism \\t\\tCoverage: 100% \\tLCD Panel \\t\\tFixed 3.2” Rear LCD \\tInternal Microphone \\tMono","Physical":"Measurements \\t\\t6.2 × 6.6 × 3.3″ / 158.0 × 167.6 × 82.6mm \\t\\t3.37 lb / 1530 g \\tAccessory Mounts: \\t\\tTripod:1x ¼-20 \\t\\tAdditional: Hot shoe","Power Supply":"Battery \\t\\tType: Canon LP-E19 \\t\\tApproximate Operating Time: Up to 1200 frames/Approximately 120 minutes of video \\t\\tApproximate Recharge Time:  170 minutes (with included Canon LC-E19 Charger)","Recording":"Media \\t\\tType: 1x CF/1x CFast \\tHigh Resolution Class Requirement \\t\\t4K: CFast 2.0 HD: Compact Flash UDMA 7 100 MB/s or faster  4K 50/59.94 may shut off after 10s when shooting to CF   \\tMulti-Slot Recording Methods \\t\\tStandard Auto Switch Card Rec. Separately Rec. to Multiple    Formats \\t\\tPhoto: JPEG, RAW Video: MJPEG (4K), MPEG-4 AVC/H.264 \\t\\tAudio: AAC, Linear PCM (Stereo) \\t\\tFile: MOV, MP4  \\tModes \\t\\t800 Mbps: 4096 × 2160 (50p/59.94p) \\t\\t500 Mbps: 4096 × 2160 (23.98p/24p/25p/29.97p) 180 Mbps (ALL-I): 1920 × 1080 (50p/59.94p) 90 Mbps (ALL-I): 1920 × 1080 (23.98p/24p/29.97p) 60 Mbps (IPB): 1920 × 1080 (50p/59.94p) 30 Mbps (IPB): 1920 × 1080 (23.98p/24p/25p/29.97p) 12 Mbps (IPB): 1920 × 1080 (25p/29.97p)  Special Recording Modes \\tHigh Frame Rate 160 Mbps (ALL-I): 1920×1080 (100p/119.9p) \\t  \\tApproximate Record Times \\t\\t800 Mbps: 0.125 Min/GB \\t\\t500 Mbps: 0.25 Min/GB \\t\\t180 Mbps: 0.62 Min/GB \\t\\t160 Mbps (HFR): 0.75 Min/GB \\t\\t90 Mbps: 1.37 Min/GB \\t\\t60 Mbps: 2.12 Min/GB \\t\\t30 Mbps: 4.12 Min/GB \\t\\t \\t Maximum Clip Length 29min 59sec","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Fixed","Sensor Size":"Full-Frame","Stabilization":"No","Viewfinder Type":"Optical","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"2.9 lb.","Wireless":"Wi-Fi \\t\\tWith optional WFT-E8A Transmitter","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi"}', '1DX
Mark
II
Strap
Body cap
LP-E19 battery
LC-E19 charger', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (685, 1, 49, 'Canon 1DX Mark III', 'canon-1dx-mark-iii', 'The Canon 1DX Mark III is a powerful DSLR built for difficult and dynamic applications, and a serious upgrade to the 1DX Mark II. Key features include:

20.1MP full-frame CMOS sensor; DIGIC X image processor
EOS iTR AF X 91-point autofocus; dual-pixel CMOS autofocus
Up to 20 fps continuous shooting in live view
DCI 4K and 5.5K RAW video capture

Third Time’s the Charm. While the Canon 1DX Mark II was a refined, almost incremental update to the original 1DX, the 1DX Mark III is a substantial improvement to its predecessor. Its newly designed 20MP full-frame CMOS sensor and DIGIC X image processor give you sharp, detailed images even when you’re shooting in low light, and improved shooting rates and video-capture capabilities. An all-new 191-point autofocus system uses “Deep Learning” to track heads and faces, and it uses Dual Pixel AF in live view for fast subject tracking. CFexpress memory compatibility caters to the improved shooting rates and higher-resolution video capabilities, and you can get twice as many shots per battery charge compared to the Mark II.

20.1MP Full-Frame CMOS Sensor. This redesigned sensor works in tandem with a newly designed low-pass filter and a DIGIC X image processor to give you remarkable image quality, speed, and sensitivity. You get up to 20 fps continuous shooting in live view or 16 fps when using the viewfinder, while the buffer gives you RAW + JPEG bursts of up to 1,000 frame sequences. The ISO 100-102,400 native sensitivity range can be expanded to 50-819,200, making the 1DX III great in a broad range of lighting conditions.

Refined EOS iTR AF X Autofocus System. A redeveloped imaging system deserves a refined autofocus system, and that’s just what you get. The EOS iTR AF X system uses 191 points—155 of which are cross-type—to quickly and accurately acquire focus, while Deep Learning Technology offers even more refined head and facial tracking for subject recognition.

Dual-Pixel CMOS AF. The Mark III also includes Canon’s dual-pixel AF system. Limited to video and live-view shooting, this system uses phase-detection for continuous autofocus and tracking with user-adjustable sensitivity and speed settings. Its 3,869 manually selectable points and 525 automatic positions give you smooth, fast focusing similar to what you’d find on a camcorder, while its Movie Servo AF mode lets you dictate tracking sensitivity, autofocus speed, and face-tracking priority. This camera also offers rack focusing via the touchscreen rear LCD when shooting video.

DCI 4K and 5.5K RAW Video. The Canon EOS-1DX Mark III captures DCI 4K video up to 60p with 10-bit 4:2:2 color, and 12-bit RAW 5.5K video. You can record DCI 4K with either the full sensor area or a cropped portion, and Canon Log Gamma gives you control over color grading. When you’re using the Canon Log setting, this camera can output 10-bit movie footage in ITU-R BT.2020 color, while the HDMI port can output 4K video directly to an external drive. The Mark III also captures Full HD up to 120p (4:2:0/8-bit) for slow-motion playback. Audio is handled by the in-camera stereo mic or externally using the 3.5mm input, with real-time monitoring possible thanks to the 3.5mm headphone jack. In addition to Canon Log Gamma, you also get Movie Digital IS, manual focus peaking, and Focus Guide, although you’ll need an external EVF or video monitor if you want zebra warnings.

Professional Build. Just as you’d expect from a 1D-series camera, the Mark III is built like a tank. The magnesium-alloy body features built-in vertical grip, dust- and weather-sealing, a touch-sensitive Smart Controller, multiple customizable buttons, bright 0.76x optical pentaprism with 100% viewfinder coverage, and a 3.2-inch, 2.1m-dot rear touchscreen LCD. It uses the same LP-E19 battery as its predecessor, but offers up to 2,850 shots per charge compared to the Mark II’s 1,210.

Dual CFexpress Memory Slots. To keep up with the increase in data flow, the Mark III takes advantage of the CFexpress format. You’ll need to use CFexpress cards if you’re looking to get the most out of the Mark III, so Canon has equipped it with dual CFexpress-compatible slots. This means you can record 5.5 RAW footage on one CFexpress card while simultaneously recording high-quality 4K MP4 video on the other.', 889000.0, '{"Accessory Shoe":"4:2:2 10-Bit\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) up to 59.94p","Aspect Ratio":"3:2","Audio File Formats":"AAC, Linear PCM (Stereo)","Audio Recording":"Built-In Microphone (Stereo)\\nExternal Microphone Input (Stereo)","Autofocus Points":"Phase Detection: 191 (155 Cross-Type)","Autofocus Sensitivity":"-4 to +18 EV","Battery":"1x LP-E19 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 11.1 VDC, 2750 mAh (Approx. 2850 Shots)","Bit Depth":"14-Bit","Brand":"Canon","Built-in Flash":"No","Camera Mount":"Canon EF","Camera Type":"DSLR","Compatible Media":"CFexpress Type B","Continuous Shooting":"Up to 20 fps at 20.1 MP for up to 1000 Exposures (RAW)\\nUp to 16 fps at 20.1 MP for up to 1000 Exposures (Raw)","Dedicated Flash System":"eTTL","Depth":"3.3\\"","Diopter Adjustment":"-3 to +1","Exposure Compensation":"-5 to +5 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)","Exposure Modes":"Aperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter Priority","External Flash Connection":"Hot Shoe, PC Terminal","Flash Compensation":"-3 to +3 EV (1/3 EV Steps)","Focusing":"Continuous-Servo AF, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AF","GPS":"Yes","Height":"6.6\\"","Image File Formats":"JPEG, Raw, HEIF","Inputs/Outputs":"USB Type-C (USB 3.1), HDMI C (Mini), Canon N3, 3.5mm Headphone, 3.5mm Microphone, PC Sync Socket, RJ45","Interval Recording":"Yes","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Frame Rate":"60","Maximum Photo Resolution":"21.4 MP","Maximum Resolution":"5472 × 3648","Maximum Sync Speed":"1/250 Second","Maximum Video Resolution":"4K","Memory Card Slot":"Dual Slot: CFexpress Type B (CFexpress 1.0)","Metering Range":"0 to 20 EV","Mfr. Model Number":"3829C019","Mirror Lock-Up":"Yes","Monitor Resolution":"2,100,000 Dot","Monitor Size":"3.2\\"","Pixels":"Actual: 21.4 Megapixel\\nEffective: 20.1 Megapixel","Recording Limit":"Up to 29 Minutes, 59 Seconds","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Fixed","Self Timer":"2/10-Second Delay","Sensor Dimensions":"36 × 24mm","Sensor Size":"Full-Frame","Shutter Speed":"Mechanical Shutter\\n1/8000 to 30 Seconds\\nBulb Mode","Stabilization":"Yes","Video Encoding":"NTSC/PAL","Video Recording Modes":"Raw 12-Bit\\n5.5K (5472 × 2886) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [1800 to 2600 Mb/s]\\n\\nMP4/H.265 4:2:2 10-Bit\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [170 to 1000 Mb/s]\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [170 to 1000 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p/100p/119.88p [18 to 470 Mb/s]\\n\\nMP4/H.264 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [120 to 940 Mb/s]\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [120 to 940 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p/100p/119.88p [12 to 360 Mb/s]","Viewfinder Coverage":"100%","Viewfinder Eye Point":"20mm","Viewfinder Magnification":"Approx. 0.76x","Viewfinder Type":"Optical","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"2.8 lb.","White Balance":"Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Custom, Daylight, Flash, Fluorescent (White), Shade, Tungsten","Width":"6.2\\"","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Canon 1DX
