Ultra-responsive joystick, 7” touchscreen control panel

Professional-Grade PTZ Camera. The Canon CR-N700 4K PTZ Camera with 15x Zoom is a professional-grade camera designed for high-end broadcast, television-studio, and live-event applications. It’s remotely controlled, so it’s especially great on productions with small crews.

One-Inch 4K CMOS Sensor and DIGIC DV7 Processor. The one-inch 4K CMOS sensor works in tandem with the DIGIC DV7 to enable professional-quality images, easy operability, and fast performance. The CR-N700 is capable of capturing UHD 4K video at 60p in up to 4:2:2 10-bit 12G-SDI and HDMI for broadcast-standard image quality. It’s also capable of outputting 4K60p over IP. Its sensor is larger than what you normally find in PTZ cameras, and it produces beautiful pro-grade images with reduced noise, high clarity, and smooth color rendering, even when you’re shooting in low light. It also gives you pleasing bokeh at large apertures.

Dual-Pixel CMOS Autofocus. The CR-N700’s Dual-Pixel CMOS Autofocus system combines imaging and phase-difference autofocus features. This system determines the focusing position by the phase difference, enabling fast, smooth focusing. Its AF tracking is effective even when you’re zooming, panning, or tilting. It incorporates EOS Intelligent Tracking and Recognition Auto Focus (EOS iTR AF) technology, which uses deep-learning autofocus technology to lock on to a subject’s head, even if they turn away from the camera.

Control Up to One Hundred Supported Cameras. The Canon RC-IP100 Touchscreen PTZ Joystick Controller uses Canon’s new XC protocol to give you IP control over 99 supported Canon PTZ cameras including the CR-N700.

Smooth PTZ Movement, Advanced Remote Functionality. The RC-IP100’s ultra-responsive joystick gives you the smooth, accurate PTZ control you need for professional productions. In addition, you can remotely control, adjust, and set the pan, tilt, and zoom functions; register up to one hundred presets per camera; and manage a range of other settings and customizations from trace movement to picture quality. The trace function can store camera movements and then recall them with the push of a button.', 5700000.0, '{"Brand":"Canon","Camera Type":"PTZ","Item Type":"Camera"}', '(3)
CR-N700
PTZ
Cameras
RC-IP100
Joystick
Controller
See
Details', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (791, 2, 49, 'Canon Cine-Servo 11-55mm T2.95-4.4 (PL)', 'canon-cine-servo-11-55mm-t2-95-4-4-pl', 'The Canon Cine-Servo 11-55mm T2.95-4.4 (PL) is a lightweight zoom lens offering Super35 coverage through its standard zoom range, and Full-Frame sensor coverage with its built-in 1.5x extender engaged. Key features include:

Versatile solution for 8K and HDR capture
Cooke/i technology; ZEISS eXtended data
16.5-82.5mm focal length with built-in extender
Upgraded V drive unit

Versatile 8K Capture. The Canon Cine-Servo 11-55mm T2.95-4.4 (PL) delivers versatility and portability in one of the shortest servo focal lengths on the market. Natively, this lens’s 11-55mm focal length and T2.95 maximum aperture work in tandem to fully support 8K PL-mount cinema cameras with Super 35 sensors. However, this lens features a built-in 1.5x extender that not only expands the focal length to 16.5-82.5mm and maximum aperture to T4.4 when engaged, but also bridges compatibility for full-frame sensors!

Standard Broadcast Interface and V Drive System. Promoting the same 12-pin camera interface for power and serial data as found on regular Canon broadcast lenses, the 11-55mm features an upgraded V Drive zoom system designed to deliver focus breathing correction and overall improved servo performance. It also has three 20-pin connectors below its servo so that you can connect a system to collect 16-bit virtual image data, and a USB-C connector to facilitate easy setup. Its 16-bit Cooke /i Technology and ZEISS eXtended Data metadata output means you can integrate it into studio systems, and you can remove the servo drive entirely if you’re shooting in a cinema style.

Cinema Construction. This lens was designed with professional production needs as its top priority. It has an 11-blade stepless aperture that produces smooth, pleasing bokeh, while its knurled focus ring features 180° rotation and includes dual film-industry 0.8 & 0.5 pitch gears for focus, zoom, and iris control.', 6386000.0, '{"Aperture":"MaximumT2.95T4.4","Brand":"Canon","Camera Connection":"Hirose 20-Pin (LANC / Cooke /i Technology Lens Data / ZEISS eXtended Lens Data) USB-C Hirose 12-Pin","Focus Type":"Manual Focus Only","Gear Standard":"0.8 MOD","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"APS-C, Full-Frame, and Super35","Lens Mount":"PL","Lens Type":"Wide Angle and Cine","Mfr. Model Number":"#7428C002","Physical":"Diameter4.5\\" Length10.6\\" Weight6.44 lb","Stabilization":"No","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', 'Canon
