INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (798, 2, 49, 'Canon Cine-Servo 17-120mm T2.95-3.9 RF', 'canon-cine-servo-17-120mm-t2-95-3-9-rf', 'The Canon Cine-Servo 17-120mm T2.95-3.9 RF is one of the first ENG-style motorized zoom lenses for the Canon RF mount. Key features include:

Supports 8K/4K cameras with native RF mount
Next-gen e-Xs V servo drive unit with ENG-style grip and zoom rocker
Perfect for RF-mount, Super 35/APS-C crop-sensor cameras
Compatible with Canon Virtual Production System

Motorized Zoom. The Canon Cine-Servo 17-120mm T2.95-3.9 RF features an ENG-style hand grip and zoom rocker on an e-Xs V servo drive unit that offers fast focus and iris speeds, Focus Breathing Compensation, and a USB-C port for saving drive unit settings and maintenance history. Power is provided by a 12-pin Hirose connector (cable available here). There are three 20-pin connectors below the servo unit for connecting third-party zoom and focus controllers or for using as a virtual terminal to output critical metadata for virtual production.

Cinema Construction. Designed for professional production needs, the lens has dual focus drive gears (0.8 & 0.5), a zoom drive gear (0.5), and an iris drive gear (0.4). The 11-blade stepless aperture produces natural, circular bokeh and a soft light beam when shooting bright subjects.

Super 35 Sensor Coverage. The Canon 17-120mm T2.95-3.9 is designed specifically for image sensors measuring 26.2 × 13.8mm and smaller. That makes it perfect for Super 35 and APS-C crop-sensor cameras, offering a focal length roughly equivalent to 27-192mm.

Suitable for VR Production. This lens is compatible with the Canon Virtual Production System and can transfer metadata for VR post-production. This is thanks, in part, to the RF mount’s high-speed communication capabilities. A high-resolution, 16-bit encoder enables precise location detection, making calibration easier when creating virtual content. Plus, the 20-pin connector can be switched to a virtual terminal to output zoom, focus, and iris position information. With compatible cameras, such as the C400, this lens provides distortion and shading data for virtual production.

Try it with These RF Mount Cameras. This lens supports Dual Pixel CMOS AF II with expanded distance measuring to make focusing easier when shooting in 4K. Only certain cameras are compatible with this lens function, such as the Canon C400 and the Canon R5 C (when in Super 35/APS-C or Super 16 modes only). Otherwise, this lens pairs with Super 35-sensor, RF-mount cameras like the Canon C70.', 3257000.0, '{"Angle of View":"71.8-44.2°","Brand":"Canon","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Mount":"Canon RF","Lens Type":"Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, Standard, and Telephoto"}', 'Canon
