INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (872, 1, 49, 'Canon EOS R6V', 'canon-eos-r6v', 'The Canon EOS R6V makes its mark as the first V-series camera equipped with a 32.5MP full-frame sensor and DIGIC X image processor designed to capture stabilized, high-quality 7K RAW footage. Key features include:

Full-size HDMI port
Dual Pixel CMOS autofocus | In-body stabilization
3-inch vari-angle touchscreen display
CFexpress Type B & SDXC UHS-II card slots

New Product – Coming Soon.

Place your reservation now! We fill orders on a first-come, first-served basis. Please note that included items and rental cost could change as we finalize this listing.

If the listed rental price increases between your preorder and ship dates, don’t worry—you’ll be locked in at your original pre-order price. And if the price decreases, you’ll still pay the lower price. We’ll always contact you to confirm pricing before we ship your order.

Rated V for Versatility. The EOS V-Series sets a new standard with its first ever 32.5MP full-frame sensor camera, the Canon EOS R6 V. Touting impressive image quality alongside video-tailored ergonomics, this camera captures up to 7K RAW footage with an impressive 15+ stops of dynamic range. The V-series is a line of compact cameras that prioritize mobile video. Despite the V designation, the EOS R6 V carries a very similar spec sheet to the EOS R6 Mark III. They both use the same full-frame sensor and Dual Pixel CMOS AF II system, and both boast unlimited recording and 40 frames-per-second shooting speeds. Where the R6 V diverges from the prior model is in its build. Designed with user feedback in mind, Canon addressed the needs of content creators with video-focused elements such as a red tally light, a red “recording border” around the LCD, two recording buttons, vertical and horizontal tripod mounts, and a zoom lever for Power Zoom compatible lenses – all in a palm-sized form factor.

A Comprehensive Hybrid Solution. Equipped with some of the popular features of the Cinema EOS line, the EOS R6 V is versatile enough for pros while still being accessible to novices, whether it’s for social media, travel, streaming, or corporate work. The EOS R6V sports Canon Log 3, HLG, PQ, 709 Recording, False Color, Zebras, and four-channel audio recording. For beginners, there are automatic movie presets including Close-up Demo (for e-commerce marketers), Smooth Skin, Movie IS (designed especially for vlogging), and Color Filter with 14 different grading options.

Complex Projects, Simplified Workflows. The aim of the EOS R6 V is wider accessibility of higher-end features presented in a simpler way. Want to explore slow motion effects? This camera placed the Slow and Fast mode right on the top dial for quick control of both the video frame rate and playback speed in-camera. Capture that cinematic look instantly with Cinema View mode, which creates a letterboxed 2.35:1 aspect ratio.

Versatile Connectivity. For both burgeoning and established streamers, this camera is equipped with 5 and 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and built-in wireless livestreaming. For livestreaming there are four options: over USB-C, with the Live Switcher app (for multi-cam setups), over micro-HDMI, or with the Camera Connect app (for remote control via smartphone). Access these options quickly with the dedicated “Live Stream” button. UVC/UAC compatibility means you can use this camera as a webcam to stream live video with the broadcasting software of your choice, directly through social media, or with video conferencing software like Zoom.

Lenses to Use with the EOS R6 V. This is an full-frame sensor camera and it will pair with both full frame and crop-frame RF-mount lenses. It has a 1.6x crop factor (with some additional cropping in certain video modes). Popular crop-sensor lenses for compact hybrid cameras like the EOS R6 V include the Canon RF 15-35mm f/2.8L IS and the Canon RF 28-70mm f/2L, both of which are just over 3" long and slightly over a pound. They also each have a ring-type Ultrasonic Motor for fast and smooth continuous autofocus performance when shooting video.', 518000.0, '{"Brand":"Canon","Built-In Flash":"No","Camera Mount":"Canon RF","Camera Type":"Mirrorless","Compatible Media":"CFexpress Type B and SD","I/O Connectivity":"HDMI, 3.5mm Headphone, 3.5mm Microphone, USB-PD, and 2.5mm LANC","ISO Range":"100 – 64000","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Burst Rate":"330","Maximum Frame Rate":"29.97 fps","Maximum Photo Resolution":"6960 × 4640","Maximum Video Resolution":"4K and 7K","Mfr. Model Number":"7250C002","Screen Size":"3\\"","Screen Type":"Touchscreen, Tilt, and Swivel","Sensor Size":"Full-Frame","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"No","Weight":"1.3 lb","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Canon
EOS
R6V', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (873, 1, 49, 'Canon EOS R7', 'canon-eos-r7', 'The Canon EOS R7 is a powerful, versatile, and sleek compact mirrorless camera that marks Canon’s entry into APS-C. Key features include:

32.5MP APS-C CMOS sensor; Dual-Pixel CMOS AF II
UHD 4K60p 10-bit video, HDR-PQ, and Canon Log 3
30 fps stills with the electronic shutter, 15 fps mechanical
Works with RF-S and full-frame RF-mount lenses

32.5MP APS-C Sensor. The Canon EOS R7’s versatile 32.5MP APS-C CMOS sensor is ideal for photo and video applications alike. It produces low-noise, high-resolution stills; UHD 4K video at 60p; UHD 4K30p when oversampled from a 7K area; and Full HD 120p video.

DIGIC X Image Processor. The DIGIC X Image Processor supports continuous shooting rates up to 30 fps with a silent electronic shutter or 15 fps with a mechanical shutter and AF and AE tracking. It also offers great low-light performance with a native ISO sensitivity of 100-32,600 that’s extendable to 100-51,200.

Lens Compatibility. From the jump, you get full compatibility with a wide range of new Canon RF and RF-S lenses. Want to use a EF or EF-S lens? Try using one of Canon’s adapters, like the Canon EF-EOS R Mount Adapter or the Canon EF-EOS R Control Ring Mount Adapter.

UHD 4K Capture. In addition to its still-shooting power, the R7 can produce high-res UHD 4K60p internal video in 10-bit with Canon Log 3 using its full sensor width. It can also use a 7K recording area for oversampled UHD 4K30p footage with improved sharpness, lower noise, and reduced moiré. You also get 120p capture at up to Full HD resolution for slow-motion playback. This camera is also capable of recording HDR-PQ, both internally and via its micro-HDMI port, which supports clean 4K output at up to 60 fps.

Dual-Pixel CMOS Autofocus II. Canon’s Dual Pixel CMOS Autofocus II system provides extremely fast and accurate live view autofocus performance. It features 651 automatic autofocus points that cover the entire sensor area. This phase-detection focusing system offers enhanced subject detection—it can recognize and track people, animals, and vehicles. The subject-detection mode is separate from the face/eye detection feature, so face/eye detection remains active even if you turn subject detection off. The AF areas include three AF zones whose size and shape you can customize.

Sensor-Shift Image Stabilization. On its own, the built-in five-axis image-stabilization system compensates for up to seven stops of camera shake, making it great for shooting hand-held at lower shutter speeds. When working in tandem with select lenses’ built-in optical image stabilization, it can compensate for up to eight stops of camera shake.

OLED Electronic Viewfinder and Touchscreen LCD. The R7’s 2.36m-dot, 1.15x-magnification OLED EVF is bright, clear, and designed for high-resolution eye-level viewing. It’s virtually lag-free and has a 120 fps refresh rate for accurate portrayal of motion. The large 3.0-inch 1.62m-dot vari-angle touchscreen LCD monitor is great for shooting, image review, and live-view monitoring. Its 180° upward and 45° downward tilting design makes it great for shooting from high and low angles.

Memory, Power, and Connectivity. This camera has dual UHS-II SDHC/XC memory-card slots, and uses the Canon LP-E6NH battery with a rated output of up to 660 shots per charge using the LCD, or up to 380 shots per charge using the EVF. There’s built-in 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity, allowing you to control the camera, review images, and transfer files from a compatible iOS/Android device with Canon’s Camera Connect app. You also get a USB Type-C 3.2 Gen 2 port, a micro-HDMI port, and 3.5mm headphone and mic ports to help with video recording.

Next-Gen Multi-Function Shoe. This updated shoe has a row of pins at the front to support more accessories than a conventional shoe and to provide power to certain types of accessories that ordinarily use separate batteries. Among other accessories, this shoe is compatible with the Canon ST-E10 Speedlite Transmitter, the Canon DM-E1D Stereo Mic, the Canon AD-P1 Smartphone Adapter, and the Canon AD-E1 Multi-Function Shoe Adapter, the last of which gives you compatibility with legacy shoe-mounted accessories.', 318000.0, '{"Brand":"Canon","Camera Mount":"Canon RF","Camera Type":"Mirrorless","Compatible Media":"SD","Environmental":"Operating Temperature32 to 104°FOperating Humidity0 to 85%","Exposure Control":"Shutter TypeElectronic Shutter, Mechanical Focal Plane ShutterMechanical Shutter Speed1/8000 to 30 SecondsElectronic Shutter Speed1/16000 to 30 SecondsBulb/Time ModeBulb ModeISO Sensitivity (Photo)100 to 32,000 in Manual, Auto Mode (Extended: 100 to 51,200)Metering MethodCenter-Weighted Average, Evaluative, Partial, SpotExposure ModesAperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityExposure Compensation-3 to +3 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)Metering Range-2 to 20 EVWhite BalancePresets: Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Custom, Daylight, Flash, Fluorescent (White), Shade, TungstenContinuous Shooting (Electronic Shutter)Up to 30 fps at 32.5 MP for up to 126 Frames (JPEG) / 42 Frames (RAW)Continuous Shooting (Mechanical Shutter)Up to 15 fps at 32.5 MP for up to 224 Frames (JPEG) / 51 Frames (RAW)Interval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/10-Second Delay","External Video Capture":"IP StreamingYes","Flash":"Built-In FlashNoMaximum Sync Speed1/320 SecondFlash Compensation-3 to +3 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)Dedicated Flash SystemeTTLExternal Flash ConnectionHot Shoe","Focusing":"Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModesContinuous-Servo AF, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AFAutofocus Points (Photo, Video)Phase Detection: 651Autofocus Sensitivity-5 to +20 EV","General":"Battery Type1x LP-E6NH Rechargeable Lithium-IonTripod Mounting Thread1 × 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Dimensions (W x H x D)5.2 × 3.6 × 3.6″Weight1.2 lbs. (Body Only)1.3 lbs. (Body with Battery and Memory Card)","Imaging":"Lens MountCanon RFSensor ResolutionActual: 34.4 MegapixelEffective: 32.5 MegapixelSensor Type22.3 × 14.8 mm (APS-C) CMOSCrop Factor1.6xImage StabilizationSensor-Shift, 5-AxisBuilt-In ND FilterNoneCapture TypeStills & Video","Inputs/Outputs":"Video I/O1x Micro-HDMI OutputAudio I/O1x 1/8\\" / 3.5 mm TRS Stereo Headphone Input1x 1/8\\" / 3.5 mm TRS Stereo Microphone OutputOther I/O1x USB Type-C (USB 3.2 / 3.1 Gen 2) Input/Output","Internal Video Capture":"H.265/MP4 4:2:2 10-Bit RecordingUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.98p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94pFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.98p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p/100p/119.88pH.264/MP4 4:2:0 8-Bit RecordingUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 23.98p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94pFull HD (1920 × 1080) up to 23.98p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p/100p/119.88pGamma CurveCanon Log 3, HDR-PQVideo SystemNTSC/PALBuilt-In Microphone TypeStereoAudio RecordingMP4: 2-Channel AAC AudioMP4: 2-Channel LPCM Audio","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Frame Rate":"100 fps","Maximum Photo Resolution":"32.5 MP","Maximum Video Resolution":"4K","Memory Card Slot":"Dual Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II)","Mfr. Model Number":"5137C002AA","Monitor":"Size3.0\\"Resolution1,620,000 DotDisplay TypeFree-Angle Tilting Touchscreen LCD","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Swivel","Sensor Size":"APS-C","Stabilization":"Yes","Still Image Capture":"Aspect Ratio1:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9Image File FormatsC-RAW, HEIF, JPEG, RAW","Viewfinder":"TypeBuilt-In Electronic (OLED)Resolution2,360,000 DotEye Point22mmCoverage100%MagnificationApprox. 1.15xDiopter Adjustment-4 to +2","Viewfinder Type":"Electronic","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.2 lb.","Wireless":"WiFi2.4 GHz Wi-Fi (802.11b/g)BluetoothGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)None","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Canon
EOS
