Hood
Dust cap', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (931, 2, 49, 'Canon RF 100-300mm f/2.8 L IS USM', 'canon-rf-100-300mm-f-2-8-l-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 100-300mm f/2.8 L IS USM is a well-rounded high-speed telephoto zoom for full-frame Canon RF-mount cameras. Key features include:

Fast, versatile telephoto zoom; RF Extender compatible
Great for indoor-sports, theater, and fashion photography
Up to six stops of image stabilization with select cameras
Fast, accurate, and silent autofocus; internal-focus design

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 100-300mm f/2.8 L IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with RF-mount cameras, but it doesn’t work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Fast, Versatile Telephoto Zoom. This lens’s versatile telephoto zoom range makes it perfect for portrait, fashion, indoor-sports, theater, and video applications. Its fast f/2.8 constant aperture and circular nine-blade diaphragm give you extensive depth-of-field control, let you work in available light, and help produce smooth, pleasing bokeh while keeping your subject sharp.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s 18-group/23-element optical formula includes 1 fluorite element, 1 aspherical element, and 4 Ultra-Low Dispersion elements to combat chromatic aberrations and color fringing throughout the zoom range while maximizing clarity, color fidelity, and sharpness. Canon has applied Air Sphere and Super Spectra coatings to each lens element to further minimize ghosting and flare, even in harsh light.

Fast, Ultra-Precise Autofocus. The Dual Nano Ultrasonic Motor (USM) autofocus system uses a combination of ring-type USM and stepping-motor (STM) mechanisms to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. There are two separate, independently actuated focusing groups to give you even greater sustained sharpness throughout the zoom range, and you get an AF/MF switch for full-time manual-focus override. You can set the focus-range limiter to the full focusing range, from 5.9 feet to infinity, or from 19.7 feet to infinity for faster performance if you’re only working with distant subjects.

Additional Focusing Features. This lens’s internal focusing and zooming design means it maintains its overall length throughout the zoom and focus ranges, which makes for faster operation. A Focus Preset button allows for pre-focusing on a particular spot, storing its focus distance, and then instantly returning to that position. Four programmable L-Fn buttons let you control a host of lens and camera functions.

Optical Image Stabilization. The 100-300mm f/2.8 L’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for 5.5 stops of camera shake so that you can shoot hand-held, in lower light, and at slower shutter speeds without worry. When you pair this lens with newer EOS R bodies that themselves feature five-axis in-body image stabilization, you get up to 6 stops of shake correction.

L-Series Design. A customizable control ring lets you adjust a range of exposure settings, including aperture, ISO, flash control, white balance, and more. A built-in rotating tripod mount lets you use this lens on a tripod or monopod, and lets you quickly switch between portrait and landscape shooting orientations. A weather-sealed build keeps you shooting in inclement conditions, and a fluorine coating on the front lens element protects against moisture, fingerprints, and debris.

Extender Compatibility. The 100-300mm is compatible with the Canon RF Extender 1.4x and 2x, each of which will extend the lens’s effective reach.', 1468000.0, '{"Angle of View":"24°-8° 15’","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"5 × 12.7″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"112mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"100-300","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"18/23","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon RF","Lens Type":"Telephoto, Supertelephoto, and For Mirrorless","Maximum Aperture":"2.8","Maximum Magnification":"0.16x","Mfr. Model Number":"6055C002","Minimum Focusing Distance":"5.9’","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"5.7lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', 'Canon 100-300mm f/2.8
Canon
ET-124 hood
Lens case', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (932, 2, 49, 'Canon RF 100-400mm f/5.6-8 IS USM', 'canon-rf-100-400mm-f-5-6-8-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 100-400mm f/5.6-8 IS USM is a versatile, relatively portable telephoto zoom for Canon RF-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Versatile, relatively portable telephoto zoom
5.5 stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, quiet, and accurate autofocus system
Customizable control ring

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 100-400mm f/5.6-8 IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF-mount cameras but does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Versatile Zoom Range. This lens’s telephoto focal range makes it perfect for sports, wildlife, and travel photography. The f/5.6-8 aperture range isn’t great for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor lighting conditions for best results.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to 5.5 stops of correction, allowing you to shoot in lower light and at lower shutter speeds without worry. When you use this lens with a camera that has an in-body image stabilizer, you get up to six stops of correction.

Nano USM Autofocus. This Nano USM autofocus system uses both a ring-type USM and an STM mechanism to ensure fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance. You also get full-time manual focusing when you’re working in one-shot AF mode.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s nine-group/twelve-element optical design includes one Ultra-Low Dispersion element and one aspherical element which combine to reduce aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering.

Although this rental will not include a hood, we do have the Canon ET-74B Hood available to add to your order!', 125000.0, '{"Angle of View":"24° to 6° 10’","Aperture Blades":"9, Rounded","Brand":"Canon","Dimensions":"ø: 3.1 x L: 6.5\\"","Filter Size":"67mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"100-400","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon RF","Lens Type":"Telephoto, Supertelephoto, and For Mirrorless","Macro Reproduction Ratio":"1:2.44","Magnification":"0.41x","Maximum Aperture":"f/5.6-8","Mfr. Model Number":"#5050C002","Minimum Aperture":"f/32 to 45","Minimum Focusing Distance":"2.9’","Optical Design":"12 Elements in 9 Groups","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"No","Weight":"1.4 lb","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', 'Canon 100-400mm f/5.6-8
Front & rear caps
