INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1091, 2, 60, 'Cooke 50mm T2.4 SP3 Full-Frame Prime (Canon RF)', 'cooke-50mm-t2-4-sp3-full-frame-prime-canon-rf', 'The Cooke 50mm T2.4 SP3 Full-Frame Prime (Canon RF) is a lightweight, high-quality Canon RF-mount cine lens that covers full-frame sensors. Key features include:

Full-frame coverage; true T2.4 aperture
Sharpness at center frame with roll-off at the edges
Color-matched to Panchro/i Classic lenses
Durable, lightweight, weather-sealed build

For Full-Frame. This Cooke 50mm T2.4 SP3 Full-Frame Prime (Canon RF) is a lightweight, cinema style lens with a true 2.4 aperture that is designed to support Full-Frame sensors. While this lens is only compatible with RF-Mount compatible cameras, like the Canon EOS R6, we do offer it in 18mm, 25mm, 75mm, and 100mm. Want ’em all? Grab one of our 5-lens or 6-lens packages!

Superlative Image Quality. Like every lens in the SP3 series, the 50mm T2.4 gives you exceptional definition and resolution in the center of the frame, with roll-off at the edges when used wide open. As you’d expect, this lens excels at rendering images of faces with lifelike skin tone and character.

Cinema Design. This lens’s cine-style aperture and focusing rings boast standard 0.8 mod gears so that you can easily install a follow-focus system, lens motor, or lens-control system, and its 64mm front diameter lets you use almost any cine-style matte box. It boasts a generous 78° of iris rotation and a 160° smooth focus throw that gives you accurate focus pulling. The nine-blade aperture gives you smooth, accurate control with even greater precision toward the wider end.

Durable, Lightweight Build. The 50mm was designed for a wide range of shooting applications including hand-held and Steadicam, and it balances comfortably when used with compact cameras. A cam-style focus mechanism ensures smooth adjustments, while large, clear numbers on both sides of the barrel give your focus puller the option of working on either side of the lens. The body boasts a scratch-resistant PTFE hard anodized finish, which increases durability so that you can shoot in inclement conditions.

Matches Cooke’s Panchro/i Classic Lenses. This lens and every lens in the SP3 series is color-matched to the Cooke Panchro/i Classic lenses, meaning that you can use the SP3s on drone- or gimbal-mounted B or C cameras.', 914000.0, '{"Angle of View":"47°","Aperture Blades":"9","Brand":"Cooke","Dimensions":"2.5 × 3.7″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"58.0mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"50-50","Focus Rotation":"160º","Focus Type":"Manual Focus Only","Front Lens Diameter":"64mm","Gearing":"0.8 MOD focus, iris","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Canon RF","Lens Type":"Standard, Cine, and For Mirrorless","Maximum Aperture":"2.4","Maximum Magnification":"0.3x","Mfr. Model Number":"15.50.7.0 (RF)","Minimum Focusing Distance":"1.29’","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.1 lb.","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Cooke 50mm
