INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1592, 1, 100, 'GoPro HERO12 Black', 'gopro-hero12-black', 'The GoPro HERO12 Black is a compact adventure camera and predecessor to the more feature-rich GoPro HERO13 Black. Key features include:

HyperSmooth 6.0 image stabilization
Front andrear LCD screens
33’ waterproof without housing
1720mAh capacity rechargeable battery

What’s New? The GoPro HERO12 Black offers a few different upgrades to its predecessor, the HERO11, including improved battery life, HyperSmooth 6.0 technology, and expanded Bluetooth capabilities. Improved HyperSmooth 6.0 image stabilization ensures more steady footage while not using a gimbal and includes horizon-lock technology that helps ensure your video is lined up properly. When you need extra support, this GoPro is compatible with the same hinge-style accessories as GoPros past and does not require a frame or case thanks to the mounting fingers that tuck into the bottom of the housing. Wondering whether a previous-gen accessory is compatible with the HERO12? Check the chart!

High Quality, HyperSmooth. With this HERO12, you have the ability to enable HDR for both photo and video to get more precise detail in your shadows and highlights. This unit will allow you to capture 5.3K60 video or up to 27MP RAW photos that are guaranteed to be crisp and detailed, and will also record 2.7K video at a 240 frame rate for playback at 8x slow motion. The upgraded HyperSmooth 6.0 now features AutoBoost, which reduces image cropping that might have a negative effect on your framing. When in motion, your image remains steady and level thanks to 360° Horizon Lock.

Bluetooth and Camera Control. Improved Bluetooth capabilities allow you to connect a microphone for more precise audio, or wireless headphones to unlock voice controls and monitor audio. The HERO12 offers two control modes: easy control for a more point-and-shoot approach, and pro control for fine tuning all settings, features, and modes, which you can then set as a preset.

Feature Rich Filming Compared to its predecessor, the HERO12 actually doubles the battery life. This adjustment allows you to record continuous 5.3K60 footage for 70 minutes or 1080p30 video for over 1.5 hours! There’s plenty of nifty features compiled into this camera, but one of the more notable features is Hindsight. This tool will capture up to 30 second of footage before you even hit record, so even if you fumble hitting record on time, there’s a good chance you still got the shot you wanted.

Same App and Shooting Options. While it’s worth noting that the Hypersmooth image-stabilization system has been improved, GoPro’s smartphone apps remain largely unchanged for the HERO12 camera and offer familiar features like TimeWarp, HDR photos, and night lapse video while letting users control shooting modes like burst and scheduled capture. Photos can still be captured in JPEG or GoPro’s RAW format.

To Wrap Things Up… This everything-proof camera makes for great content creation whether you’re biking the trails or swimming the seas. It’s weatherproof, waterproof up to 33 feet, and even the included battery features improved cold temperature performance. There are plenty of more advanced features available with the HERO12, like being able to choose between 8-bit or 10-bit color for smoother gradations in your footage, a HyperView digital lens that will take the 8:7 aspect ratio footage recorded by the new image sensor and deliver it as a wide-angle 16:9 shot, and the ability to connect your camera directly to your home Wi-Fi and automatically upload all recorded footage to the cloud.

Add-On Mounting Available. To expand mounting opportunities for this rental, we have the GoPro Mounts and Parts Grab Bag available separately.', 146000.0, '{"Brand":"GoPro","Camera":"Image SensorSize-Unspecified CMOS Sensor ResolutionEffective: 27 Megapixel","Camera Type":"Action","Compatible Media":"microSD","Display":"Display TypeFixed Touchscreen LCD Display Size2.27\\" Resolution368 × 552 Secondary DisplayFront: 1.4\\" LCD Live-View Monitor Shutter Speed1/8 to 30 Seconds in Photo Mode1/480 to 1/30 Second in Video Mode","Exposure Control":"ISO Sensitivity\\nPhoto100 to 3200Video100 to 6400 Shooting ModesHDRNightStar TrailsSuper Slow Motion MovieTime-Lapse Movie Remote ControlNone","Features":"Image StabilizationDigital Environmental ProtectionAdvertised as Submersible to 33’\\nTest Methodology Not Supplied Creative EffectsYes Built-In MicNo Built-In SpeakerNo Built-In Light/FlashLight – NoFlash – No WirelessBluetooth Mobile App CompatibleYes: iOS OnlyApp Name: GoPro Quik\\nAs of August, 2023: Check with manufacturer for the most up-to-date compatibility Accessory ShoeNone Tripod Mounting Thread1/4\\"-20 Female","General":"BatteryRechargeable Battery Pack, 1720 mAh Charging MethodUSB Power Adapter5 VDC Dimensions (W x H x D)2.8 × 2 × 1.3″ Weight5.4 oz","Inputs/Outputs":"Inputs1 x USB-C 3.0 / 3.1/3.2 Gen 1 Video OutputNone Microphone InputNo Headphone JackNo","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Video Resolution":"5K","Optics":"35mm-Equivalent Focal Length16.5 to 24.4mm Fixed FocusNo","Recording":"Media/Memory Card SlotSingle Slot: microSD/microSDHC (UHS-I) [512 Maximum / U3/V30 or Faster Recommended] Video Format5312 × 2988 at 60 fps (MP4 via H.265/HEVC)3840 × 2160 at 100/120 fps (MP4 via H.265/HEVC)2704 × 1520 at 200/240 fps (MP4 via H.265/HEVC)1920 × 1080p at 200/240 fps (MP4 via H.265/HEVC) Still Image SupportRaw\\n27 MP IP StreamingH.265\\n1920 × 1080","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Fixed","Sensor Size":"1-Inch","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Wireless