INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1601, 1, 100, 'GoPro MAX 360', 'gopro-max-360', 'The GoPro MAX 360 action camera is GoPro’s second attempt at 360-degree video after the GoPro Fusion and is capable of spherical video capture up to 4992 × 2496 at 30 fps to one microSDXC memory card. Key features include:

Dual 180-degree fisheye lenses with an 8.9mm focal length
360-degree video up to 4992 × 2496 at 30 fps in H.265 (HEVC)
Internal stitching with no post processing required
Records to a single microSDXC card up to 128GB

GoPro Fusion Successor. Lets get this out of the way. The GoPro MAX is better in every way than the GoPro’s previous 360-video attempt, the GoPro Fusion. The MAX adds a single microSD card with internal stitching, single camera options, and true Ambisonics audio capture.

Internally-Stitched, 5K, 360-Degree Video. The main purpose of the GoPro MAX is to record spherical 360-degree video in as simple a manner as possible. A single microSD card and internal stitching goes a long way to make this a reality. The 4992 × 2496 resolution video is sufficient for VR headsets and 2D screens, but keep in mind that the MAX is still considered entry level, and there are higher quality options like the Insta360 Pro 2 or Insta360 Titan.

Single Camera Video & Photo Modes. The MAX has a HERO mode that makes single lens recording easy, but recording resolutions are much more limited than an actual GoPro Hero8 Black. The only available options are limited to 1440p or 1080p up to 60fps. The MAX also features a photo mode for single shot panoramics and standard 360 or cropped photo capture.

Other Notable Features. This camera has upgrades over the HERO8 in both TimeWarp and horizon leveling thanks to the spherical view of the camera. HyperSmooth stabilization is at least comparable and GoPro and features like live streaming and an app for tweaking settings and making simple video edits. The camera is powered by one GoPro ACBAT-011 Enduro Battery for up to 2 hours when shooting 1080p60 video, just over 1.5 hours when shooting 1440p video, and just over an hour when shooting 5.6K video.

Add-On Mounting Available. To expand mounting opportunities for this rental, we have the GoPro Mounts and Parts Grab Bag available separately.', 239000.0, '{"360 Stitched Video Recording":"Video Stitching Resolution5K (4992 × 2496)Photo Stitching Resolution5.7K (5760 × 2880)Internal/External StitchingInternal, External Stitching360 Stitched Video Format (External 2D)4992 × 2496 at 25, 30 fps2880 × 1920 at 50, 60 fpsStill Image SupportPNG (5760 × 2880)Number of Lenses2","Audio":"6 mic array (Ambisonics)","Brand":"GoPro","Camera Type":"360","Compatible Media":"microSD","Exposure Control":"Shutter Speed1/28000 to 1/5 Seconds in Photo Mode1/50000 to 1/2 Seconds in Video ModeISO Sensitivity (Photo)100 to 800ISO Sensitivity (Video)400 to 6400SizeNot Specified by Manufacturer","General":"Waterproof Depth Rating16.0’ / 4.8m (Camera)Wi-FiYesTripod Mounting ThreadNoneBatteryRechargeable Lithium-Ion Battery Pack, 3.85 VDC, 1600 mAhCharging MethodUSB","Inputs/Outputs":"InputsNoneOutputsUSB 3.0 Type C","Item Type":"Camera","Lens":"Quantity2Focal Length8.9mmAngle of View180-degrees (per lens)","Maximum Video Resolution":"5K","Physical":"Weight5.75 ozDimensions2.5 × 2.7 × 1.6″","Recording":"Media/Memory Card SlotSingle Slot: microSD/microSDHC/microSDXC [256 GB Maximum]Built-In MicYesChannels6.0-Channel Surround","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Fixed","Sensor Size":"1-Inch","Stabilization":"Yes","Video Format":"4992 × 2496 (MP4 via H.264/AVC)","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'MAX 360 camera
