INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1963, 2, 134, 'Leitz Cine THALIA MAKRO 55mm T2.8 (PL)', 'leitz-cine-thalia-makro-55mm-t2-8-pl', 'The Leitz Cine THALIA 55mm T2.8 is a premium-quality cinema prime designed for PL-mount digital cinema cameras. It covers sensors up to 65mm and produces a distinct vintage-film look. Key features include:

PL-mount 55mm cine lens
Covers 65mm, full-frame, VistaVision, & Super 35 sensors
Produces filmic images characteristic of a vintage lens
Fifteen-blade aperture for cinematic bokeh effect

Versatile PL-Mount Cine Lens. You can use the Leitz Cine THALIA MAKRO 55mm T2.8 – and every PL-mount lens in Leitz’s THALIA series – on PL-mount professional cine cameras with 65mm, full-frame, VistaVision, and Super 35 sensors, such as the Sony VENICE 2, ARRI ALEXA LF, and ARRI ALEXA 35.

Lens Consistency. A defining characteristic of the THALIA line of lenses is their sharp, focused center with gradual focus fall-off curve toward the edges, which gives images an added depth and dimension, particularly on larger sensors. All of the THALIA lenses have 92mm filter threads (except for the 24mm), rear filter net holders, 95mm front diameters that let you use standard matte boxes, 270° smooth focus throw for accurate focus pulling with minimal focus breathing, and 0.8 mod gears so that you can easily install a follow-focus system. These common features make THALIA-series lenses easily interchangeable in the middle of your shoot.

Unique Vintage-Film Look. While the Leitz THALIAs aren’t vintage lenses, they produce many appealing image characteristics that are similar to vintage Leica S lenses. They’re all clear without being overly sharp, and they have smooth and forgiving focus without ever looking soft. They render even, natural, color-accurate skin tones.

Cinematic Bokeh and Magnification. Each of the THALIA lenses boasts a fifteen-blade aperture that maintains a circular iris through all aperture stops. This produces an extremely pleasing cinematic bokeh effect in which out-of-focus elements of your shot maintain their structure. A magnificent 1:2 magnification captures immersive and detailed close-ups.', 2643000.0, '{"Angle of View":"52.4° (Super 65), 36.2° (Full Frame), 25.5° (Super 35)","Brand":"Leitz","General":"Dimensions (ø x L)3.7 × 6.1″Weight3.6 lb.Gearing0.8 MOD270° FocusFront Lens Diameter95mm","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Mount":"PL","Lens Type":"Standard","Max Magnification":"0.5x","Mfr. Model Number":"11454-001","Min Focusing Distance":"11.8\\"","Optical Design":"Groups/ElementsN/AAperture Blades15Image Circle60mmFormat65mm"}', 'Leitz
