	77mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2226, 2, 167, 'Nikon 24mm f/1.8G ED AF-S', 'nikon-24mm-f-1-8g-ed-af-s', 'The Nikon 24mm f/1.8G ED AF-S is a budget-friendly wide-angle lens designed for Nikon FX full-frame DSLRs. Key features include:

84º angle of view
Fast, nearly silent autofocus with manual focus
Great for architecture, landscape, and street shooting
FX and DX compatible

Wide-Angle Prime. Generally speaking, 24mm is the most common wide-angle focal length due to its balance of angle of view (84º) with minimal barrel distortion. It’s a popular choice for architecture, landscape, and street photography, but it can also be useful in any instance in which you need a true wide angle but don’t want massive distortion. While it was designed with full-frame FX cameras in mind, it’s also fully compatible with crop-sensor DX cameras with a focal length equivalent to 36mm.

Fast Aperture. The f/1.8 aperture offers depth-of-field control for creating subject/background isolation, as well as enabling low-light shooting.

Silent Wave Autofocus Motor. The Silent Wave Motor provides fast, nearly silent autofocus performance. The rear-focusing design plays well with filters, as the barrel doesn’t extend or rotate. The lens offers full-time manual focus capabilities for quick manual-focus adjustment.

High-Quality Optics. There are two extra-low dispersion elements and two aspherical glass elements that combat chromatic aberrations and distortion while maximizing image sharpness, clarity, and color accuracy.', 161000.0, '{"Angle of View":"84°","Brand":"Nikon","Dimensions":"Length: 3.27\\"","Filter Style":"Nonrotating front element","Focusing System":"Rear, Full time active, SWM motor","Groups/Elements":"9/12","Hood Included":"Yes","Hood Type":"HB-76","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Mount":"Nikon F","Lens Type":"Wide Angle","Maximum Magnification":"0.2x","Mfr. Model Number":"20057","Weather Resistant":"No"}', 'Nikon 24mm
Front & rear caps
HB-76 hood
	72mm protective filter
Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2227, 2, 167, 'Nikon 24mm f/3.5D PC-E', 'nikon-24mm-f-3-5d-pc-e', 'The Nikon 24mm f/3.5D PC-E is an ultra-wide perspective-control lens. Key features include:

Great for architectural and nature photography
Extensive perspective-control options
8.4” minimum focusing distance
DX and FX compatible

The Nikon 24mm f/3.5D PC-E is an ultra-wide perspective-control (PC) lens featuring 8.5° tilt, 11.5mm shift, and 90° rotation capabilities, allowing complete perspective control.

It’s perfect for architectural and nature photography, and with 3 ED glass elements and Nano Crystal Coating, it’s amazingly sharp and flare resistant.

Please note that mastering a perspective-control lens isn’t something that can be accomplished in an hour or two. If you don’t have experience with this type of lens, you’ll need a day or two with the manual to practice before tackling an important assignment.', 268000.0, '{"Angle of View":"84º","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Nikon","Dimensions":"3.3 × 4.3″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"77.0mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"24-24","Focus Type":"Manual Focus Only","Groups/Elements":"10/13","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Nikon F","Lens Type":"Wide Angle, Tilt-Shift, and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"3.5","Maximum Magnification":"0.37x","Mfr. Model Number":"2168","Minimum Focusing Distance":"8.27\\"","Stabilization":"No","Tilt/Shift":"± 8.5° tilt\\n± 11.5mm shift","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"1.6 lb.","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Nikon 24mm f/3.5D
