INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2326, 2, 167, 'Nikon Z 180-600mm f/5.6-6.3 VR', 'nikon-z-180-600mm-f-5-6-6-3-vr', 'The Nikon Z 180-600mm f/5.6-6.3 VR is an exceptionally sharp super-telephoto zoom for Nikon Z-Mount cameras. Key features include:

Only for Nikon Z-mount cameras
Great for sports and wildlife photography
Advanced optical design for maximum sharpness
Fast, silent autofocus; 5.5 stops of vibration reduction

Nikon Z System. The Nikon Z 180-600mm f/5.6-6.3 VR was designed specifically for cameras in Nikon’s Z-mount system. Z-mount lenses only work with Z-mount cameras, and Z-mount cameras are only compatible with Z-mount lenses.

Expansive Super-Telephoto Zoom. With full-frame sensor coverage, this lens’s versatile 180-600mm focal length is ideal for sports and wildlife photography. It covers an expansive super-telephoto focal length to let you capture exciting action shots while still maximizing image quality and speed.

High-Quality Optics. The Nikon Z 180-600mm’s 17-group/25-element optical design features six extra-low dispersion elements and one aspherical element to promote sharpness and color rendering while limiting chromatic aberrations. Nikon has applied an FLC fluorine coating to the elements to combat ghosting and lens flare, even when you’re working in bright or backlit conditions.

Variable Aperture. The variable f/5.6-6.3 aperture isn’t useful for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor-lighting conditions for best results. The rounded nine-blade diaphragm contributes to smooth, pleasing bokeh for shallow depth-of-field techniques.

Vibration Reduction. The built-in vibration reduction provides up to 5.5 stops of correction for minimizing camera shake at slower shutter speeds and producing sharper results when shooting hand-held.

Stepping Motor Autofocus System. The stepping motor allows for fast, silent, and smooth operation. Pairing a speedy AF system together with a continuous manual mechanism allows you to hit your focus with confidence, while the internal-focusing design means that the lens maintains its length during focusing. A 4.3-foot minimum focusing distance and 0.25x maximum magnification at the 180mm position let you get in reasonably close to capture details.

Advanced Build. This lens’s durable, moisture-resistant construction means you can use it in adverse conditions without worry. A programmable control ring and function buttons let you adjust manual focus, aperture, or exposure compensation, among other functions.', 393000.0, '{"Angle of View":"9° to 2° 40’","Aperture Blades":"9, Rounded","Brand":"Nikon","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focus Type":"Autofocus","General":"Dimensions (ø x L) – lens only4.3 × 12.4″ / 110 × 315.5mmWeight – lens only4.3 lb. / 1.95 kg","Hood Included":"Yes","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Nikon Z","Lens Type":"Supertelephoto","Macro Reproduction Ratio":"1:4","Maximum Magnification":"0.25x","Mfr. Model Number":"20117","Optical Design":"Groups/Elements17/25Extra-Low Dispersion Elements6Aspherical Elements1","Stabilization":"Yes","Tripod Collar":"Removable and Rotating","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Zoom Type":"Variable Focal Length"}', 'Nikon 180-600mm f/5.6-6.3
