INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2413, 2, 179, 'OM SYSTEM M.Zuiko 12-40mm f/2.8 ED PRO II', 'om-system-m-zuiko-12-40mm-f-2-8-ed-pro-ii', 'The M.Zuiko 12-40mm f/2.8 ED PRO II is a fast normal-range zoom for Micro 4/3 cameras, an update to the Olympus 12-40mm f/2.8 ED PRO, and a continuation of the Olympus legacy following the OM SYSTEM rebranding. Key features include:

Excellent for portrait, wedding, and event photography
Advanced optical design for sharp, color-accurate images
Fast, quiet, and precise autofocus; full-time manual focus
Durable, weather-resistant construction

Fast Normal-Range Zoom. With a 35mm-equivalent focal length of 24-80mm, the OM SYSTEM 12-40mm f/2.8 ED PRO II covers the wide-angle to portrait-length range. Its focal length and quick f/2.8 aperture make it ideal for portraiture, event and wedding photography, and shooting in low light.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s complex nine-group/fourteen-element design includes two Extra-Low Dispersion elements, two aspherical elements, one Dual Super Aspherical element, one Extra-Low Dispersion aspherical element, and two High-Refractive Index elements. All of the elements work together to produce incredible sharpness, contrast, and color accuracy across the entire zoom range while reducing color fringing, spherical aberrations, and distortions. Each element has a Zuiko Extra-Low Reflection Optical (ZERO) coating to help reduce flare and promote optimal color transmission.

Movie and Still Compatible Autofocus System. The MSC autofocus system and internal-focusing design offer fast, quiet, and precise focusing performance that’s great for stills and video capture. You can use the MF clutch to quickly switch to manual-focus mode for more precision adjustments, and a floating zoom mechanism gives you a 7.9-inch minimum focus distance so you can get in close.

High-Quality Build. Pro-grade means pro build, and that’s what you’re getting here. The dust-, freeze-, and splash-proof barrel keeps you shooting in conditions down to -14° F. A Fluorine coating keeps dust, dirt, rain, snow, and other debris off the front element for easy cleaning.', 243000.0, '{"Angle of View":"84° 30’","Brand":"OM SYSTEM","Hood Included":"Yes","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Mount":"Micro 4/3","Lens Type":"Wide Angle and Standard","Maximum Magnification":"0.3x","Mfr. Model Number":"V335030BW000","Minimum Aperture":"22.0","Optical Design":"Groups/Elements: 9/14\\n\\nExtra-Low Dispersion Elements: 2\\n\\nAspherical Elements: 2\\n\\nDual Super Aspherical Elements: 1\\n\\nExtra-Low Dispersion Aspherical Elements: 1\\n\\nHigh-Refractive Index Elements: 2\\n\\nAperture Blades: 7, Rounded","Physical":"Dimensions (ø x L): 2.8 × 3.3″\\n\\nWeight: 0.8 lb."}', 'OM
System 12-40mm f/2.8
Front & rear caps
LH-66 hood
	62mm protective filter
Lens pouch', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2414, 2, 179, 'OM SYSTEM M.Zuiko 150-400mm f/4.5 TC 1.25 IS PRO', 'om-system-m-zuiko-150-400mm-f-4-5-tc-1-25-is-pro', 'The OM SYSTEM 150-400mm f/4.5 TC 1.25 IS PRO is a supertelephoto 300-800mm equivalent zoom for Micro 4/3-mount cameras. Key features include:

Integrated 1.25x teleconverter for a 375-1000mm equivalent range
f/4.5 max aperture throughout range, f/5.6 with teleconverter applied
8 stops of image stabilization, 4.5 with teleconverter applied
Movie & Still Compatible quiet autofocus

Ideal Sports and Wildlife Lens. Weighing in at only 4.1 pounds, this supertelephoto is incredibly portable for the length you get – up to 1000mm with the built-in teleconverter! What’s more is that this lens is also compatible with the MC-14 and MC-20 teleconverters, allowing you ultimate reach that’s customizable out in the field.

Advanced Feature Set and Optics. Using leading-edge optical technology, the 150-400mm IS PRO ensures edge-to-edge sharpness, a bright f/4.5 constant maximum aperture (f/5.6 when the teleconverter is applied), and reduced color fringing, ghosting, and flaring. The teleconverter not only gives you extra reach but it also provides a max image magnification of 0.57×. This, combined with a 4-foot shooting distance, makes this lens suitable for certain macro subjects — a unique feature for a supertelephoto lens. This lens also supports the focus stacking feature in compatible OM-System cameras. Five function switches give you options over how your lens performs: AF Limiter, AF/MF toggle, IS toggle, Electronic Sound Off, and the programmable L-Fn button, which allows for lens-based control over shooting settings.

Robust and Reliable Construction Fully weathersealed, the 150-400mm IS PRO  is ready to take on the elements. The durable magnesium alloy and carbon fiber lens body is portable despite its long range thanks in part to the internal zoom, which keeps the lens at just over a foot. It is evenly balanced so that it can be hand-held out in the field.

Try it with These Micro 4/3 Cameras This lens pairs with Micro 4/3-mount cameras with Micro 4/3 sensors. Since it is designed with sports and wildlife in mind, it is a great choice for quick shooters like the Olympus OM-D E-M1 Mark III and the Panasonic GH6 or the long-lasting Olympus OM-D E-M1X.', 1629000.0, '{"Angle of View":"8.2-3.1°","Brand":"OM SYSTEM","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Mount":"Micro 4/3","Lens Type":"Supertelephoto"}', 'OM
