Need a higher-capacity battery? Check out the Panasonic AG-VBR118G.

Need a one-stop power solution? Take a look at the Panasonic AG-VBR118G Dolgin Power Kit.

The Panasonic AG-VBR59P is a 5900 mAh battery that works with:

Panasonic AG-CX10 4K Camcorder w/ NDI Upgrade
	Panasonic AU-EVA1
	Panasonic AG-CX350 4K
	Panasonic AG-CX350 4K w/ NDI Upgrade
	Panasonic HC-X1000 4K Camcorder
	Panasonic HC-X2000 UHD 4K Camcorder
	Panasonic LUMIX BGH1 Cinema 4K
	Panasonic AG-BRD50P Dual Battery Charger
	Dolgin TC400 Four Position Charger for Panasonic AG-VBR', 93000.0, '{"Brand":"Panasonic","Item Type":"Power","Power Type":"Battery"}', 'Just the battery', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2514, 3, 183, 'Panasonic AJ-WM50P Dual-Band Wireless Module', 'panasonic-aj-wm50p-dual-band-wireless-module', 'The Panasonic AJ-WM50P Dual-Band Wireless Module is a versatile wireless solution allowing remote operation of compatible Panasonic camcorders through their respective ROP app. Key features include:

Wide range of Panasonic camcorder compatibility
Wireless function and menu control with smart device
2.4GHz and 5GHz Wi-Fi bands for better connectivity
Smart device and external monitor not included

Dual-Band. This wireless module operates on 2.4GHz and 5GHz bands, improving signal strength and reliability, even around various other wireless devices.

Compact Design. The AJ-WM50P is a small wireless module that fixes to compatible Panasonic cameras through the USB Host terminal. Most camcorders feature a thin protective cover for discrete and protected use.

Panasonic Compatibility. The range of features made remotely accessible by this wireless module is as varied as the camera systems for which it is compatible. Most camera models are limited to single camera control functions, though the CX350 is able to connect up to eight cameras for switchable single camera control. For questions regarding camera compatibility you may refer to your camera model’s manual or contact us to discuss the particular needs of your shoot.

Smart Device Required. The Panasonic ROP apps are available for most iOS devices but there is limited Android compatibility at this time. Please refer to the Resources section of this page to determine whether or not your device is approved for remote control. If you need an iOS device, we also offer the Apple iPad Mini 4 and the Apple iPad Mini 5 as a separate rental items.

Monitor Not Included. To take advantage full advantage of the AJ-WM50P features, we recommend using an external monitor (not included) for playback and menu reference.', 75000.0, '{"Brand":"Panasonic","Camera Support Type":"Wireless Adapter","Item Type":"Camera Support"}', 'Just the
AJ-WM50P', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2515, 1, 183, 'Panasonic AU-EVA1 Compact 5.7K Super 35 Cinema Camera', 'panasonic-au-eva1-compact-5-7k-super-35-cinema-camera', 'The Panasonic AU-EVA1 Compact 5.7K Super 35 Cinema Camera is a flexible, high-quality cinema camera system. Key features include:

17.25MP Dual Sensitivity 5.7K S35 sensor
Internal 4:2:2 10-bit in 4K DCI, UHD, and full HD
MOV or AVCHD (4:2:0 8-bit) recording options or output RAW
Netflix approved camera

5.7K Image Sensor. The Panasonic AU-EVA1 Compact 5.7K Super 35 Cinema Camera is based around a high-resolution 5.7K sensor that can produce oversampled 4K footage. This gives you sharper images and more accurate colors than native 4K sensors.

Dual Native ISO. The 5.7K sensor incorporates Dual Native ISO, which increases sensitivity and maintains a high signal-to-noise ratio. This camera’s standard native ISO is 800, but you can switch it to 2500 if you’re shooting in low light.

V-Log and V-Gamut Capture. The EVA1 includes both V-Log and V-Gamut capture. The former gives you curve characteristics similar to those of negative film, while the latter produces a color space that’s larger than film. The inclusion of V-Log and V-Gamut lets you use the EVA1 in HDR and SDR production workflows.

Recording Modes. The EVA1 offers up to 10-bit 4:2:2 sampling, even at 4K resolutions. You can capture in-camera footage in 4K (4096 × 2160), UHD (3840 × 2160), 2K (2048 × 1080), Full-HD (1920 × 1080), and HD (1280 × 720). The EVA1 also gives you up to 59.94 fps for 4K, up to 120 fps for 2K and Full-HD, or 240 fps with an image sensor crop.

Records to SDXC Cards. This camera records to V60-rated SD cards (not included), which support all of its internal recording modes—even the 10-bit 4:2:2 AK modes. You get two card slots so that you can simultaneously record to two cards or continuously record from card to card.

Electronic Image Stabilization. The EVA1’s built-in image-stabilization system helps keep your images clear and sharp, even when you’re shooting hand-held or shoulder-mounted.

EF Lens Mount. This camera’s EF lens mount supports a wide array of popular manufacturers’ lenses. You can view a Panasonic-verified list of compatible lenses here. Please note that the auto-iris function may have more noise than what is acceptable in some shooting situations, causing Panasonic to recommend manual iris only for many compatible lenses.

Additional Features. The EVA1 offers a range of imaging tools, including Waveform, Zebras, and Peaking. It gives you focus squares to help you achieve critical focus. You get dual XLR audio inputs; independently adjustable, 4K-capable HDMI and SDI video outputs; and timecode functionality. Finally, there are integrated, motorized ND and IR-cut filters.

Need a Memory Card? You’ll need an ultra-fast memory card for a camera this powerful, and we recommend the Sony 128GB SF-G Tough Series UHS-II SDXC. This camera can take full advantage of its superior 299 MB/s max write speed and 300 MB/s max read speed for high-resolution, high-bitrate capture.', 643000.0, '{"Brand":"Panasonic","Camera Mount":"Canon EF","Camera Type":"Cinema","Compatible Media":"SD","Imaging":"Maximum Resolution \\t\\tDCI 4K (4096 × 2160)  \\tSensor \\t\\tType: Super 35, MOS \\t\\tSize: 24.60mm x 12.97mm Effective Pixels: Approximately 17.25 MP \\tCrop Factor x 1.15 (S35 mode) \\tBit Depth4:2:2 10 bit (MOV)4:2:0 8 bit (MOV/AVCHD) \\tISO \\t\\tDynamic Range: 14 stops \\t\\tDefault Sensitivity Range: 200 to 2000 (800 base)/1000 to 25600 (2500 base) \\t\\tExpanded Sensitivity Range: (values) \\t\\tNative ISO: 800/2500 (dual) FiltersElectrical Driven ND (0.6ND, 1.2ND, 1.8ND)IR Cut Filter","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Video Resolution":"5K","Physical":"Dimensions (W x H x D) 135 × 133 × 170mm WeightBody Only: 2.65 lbsBody with Accessories: 4.5 lbs. \\tAccessory Mounts: Tripod: 1x ¼-20 and 1x ⅜-16 Additional: Cold shoe mount","Power Supply":"AC AdapterSAE0011 (included) \\tBattery \\t\\tType: AG-VBR59P (included)/AG-VBR118G (available as a separate rental item) \\t\\tOperating Time: Approximately 90 min (AG-VBR59P)/215 min. (AG-VBR118G) \\t\\tRecharge Time: Approximately 200 min. (AG-VBR59P)/300 min. (AG-VBR118G)","Recording":"Formats \\t\\tVideo: H.264/MPEG-4 AVC High Profile \\t\\tAudio: 48 kHz/24 bit 2 CH, Linear PCM (MOV), 48 kHz/16 bit, 2 CH, Dolby Audio™ (AVCHD) \\t\\tFile: MOV, AVCHD  \\t MOV Modes \\t\\t400 Mbps 422Intra: 4096 × 2160/3840 × 2160 (23.98p, 29.97p)  150 Mbps 422LongGOP: 4096 × 2160/3840 × 2160 (23.98p, 29.97p) 150 Mbps 420LongGOP: 4096 × 2160/3840 × 2160 (59.94p) 100 Mbps 420LongGOP: 4096 × 2160/3840 × 2160/204 (23.98p, 29.97p)  200 Mbps 422Intra: 2048 × 1080/1920 × 1080 (59.94p) 100 Mbps 422Intra: 2048 × 1080 (23.98p, 29.97p)/1920 × 1080 (23.98p, 29.97p, 59.94i)  100 Mbps 422LongGOP: 2048 × 1080/1920 × 1080 (59.94p) 50 Mbps 422LongGOP: 2048 × 1080 (23.98p, 29.97p)/1920 × 1080 (23.98p, 29.97p, 59.94i) \\tMedia \\t\\tType: 2 slot SD \\t\\tHigh Resolution Class Requirement: Class V60 or faster  \\tApproximate Record Times \\t\\t400 Mbps: Approximately 0.3 Min/GB 150 Mbps: Approximately 0.86 Min/GB 100 Mbps: Approximately 1.4 Min/GB 50 Mbps: Approximately 2.5 Min/GB   \\tMulti-Slot Recording Methods \\t\\tSimul RecRelay Rec","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Swivel","Sensor Size":"Super35","Stabilization":"Yes","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi"}', 'Panasonic
