INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2552, 1, 183, 'Panasonic GH5S', 'panasonic-gh5s', 'The Panasonic GH5S is a video-focused update to the pro-grade, hybrid photo/video camera. For an updated option focused on live-streaming, check out the GH5 II. Key features include:

10.28MP, low-light optimized MOS sensor
Internal DCI 4K/60p with no sensor crop or time limit
Dual native ISO at ISO 400 & ISO 2500
Internal 4:2:2 10-bit and preinstalled V-Log L gamma curve

What’s New? The GH4 was quite advanced for a hybrid photo/video mirrorless camera, and the GH5 does everything it did but better. Now, the GH5S addresses the video specific complaints of the users of Panasonic’s pro-grade, micro 4/3 camera system with a low-light optimized 10.28MP sensor, dual native ISO, improved auto-focus, 1080p at 240 fps, & time-code in/out. Notably missing from the GH5S is in-camera image stabilization.

10.28MP, Low-Light Optimized Sensor. The biggest differentiator between this camera and the base GH5 is the new 10.28 megapixel sensor. Fewer and larger pixels take in more light and double its ISO sensitivity to 51,200. Dual native ISO of 400 & 2500 extends dynamic range in more shooting situations, especially when paired with the GH5S’s preinstalled V-Log L.

DCI 4K At 60 Frames Per Second. Even with the reduced resolution of the sensor, Panasonic made sure users can still shoot in DCI and UHD 4K. The camera supports 4K/60p in 4:2:0 8-bit, but drop the frame rate to 30p for glorious 4K 4:2:2 10-bit at 400Mbps. High frame rate shooting gets a boost to 240 fps in 1080p.

V-Log L Upgrade Pre-Installed. Panasonic did everyone a solid and decided to preinstall the V-Log L upgrade on all GH5S cameras. This provides an extremely flat gamma curve and image that’s capable of 12-stops of dynamic range for additional latitude when grading your footage.

But What About Still Photography? While headlining feature upgrades are primarily video-centric, the GH5S adds 14-bit raw for photos and at 14 fps. The improved Depth From Defocus system offers faster, more accurate performance in low-light situations with sensitivity from -5 EV. We wouldn’t recommend this over other cameras for print work, but these additions will be welcome for web-centric shooters.

Timecode In/Out.  What? BNC Timecode in or out on a mirrorless camera? Panasonic added this feature, usually only found on professional camcorder systems, by way of a sync port to BNC converter cable. We don’t include the adapter cable by default. If you need it, let us know in the special instructions when you place your order.

Need a Memory Card? You’ll need an ultra-fast memory card for a camera this powerful, and we recommend the Sony 128GB SF-G Tough Series UHS-II SDXC. This camera can take full advantage of its superior 299 MB/s max write speed and 300 MB/s max read speed for high-resolution, high-bitrate capture.', 268000.0, '{"Brand":"Panasonic","Camera Mount":"Micro 4/3","Camera Type":"Mirrorless","Compatible Media":"SD","Flash":"Maximum Sync Speed1 / 250 SecondFlash Compensation3 EV to +3 EV (in 1/3 EV steps)Flash SystemDedicated: TTLConnection: Hot Shoe/PC Terminal","Imaging":"Maximum Resolution10.28MP3×2: 3680 × 276016×9: 4016 X 2256SensorType: Digital Single Lens MirrorlessSize: 17.3 × 13.0mmCrop Factorx2Bit Depth4:2:2 10 bit (external recorder required for 4K 50p/60p)4:2:0 8 bitISODynamic Range: Up to 14 stopsDefault Sensitivity Range: 160 – 51200Expanded Sensitivity Range: 80 – 204800Dual Native ISO: 400/2500","Inputs/Outputs":"Audio Input 3.5mm stereo mini-jack Audio Output 3.5mm stereo mini-jack Video Output HDMI (Full) Additional Inputs/Outputs Remote: 2.5mm LANC mini-jack Flash Synchro Socket: Flash synchronization/BNC TC conversion","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Video Resolution":"4K","Monitoring":"LCD PanelTFT LCD monitor with static touch controlFree-angle 3.2-inch  ViewfinderOLED Live View Finder Eye Sensor Internal Microphone Stereo","Physical":"Measurements5.45 × 3.86 × 3.44 inch 1.46 lbsAccessory MountsTripod: ¼-20 InsetHot shoe adapter","Power Supply":"AC AdapterDMW-AC10 AC adapter with DMW-DCC12 DC coupler (not included)BatteryType: DMW-BLF19 (supplied)Operating Time: Approximately 65 Mins. of videoRecharge Time: Approximately 190 Mins.","Recording":"Formats Photo: JPEG, RAW Video: H.264/MPEG-4 AVC, H.265/HEVC, AVCHD Progressive Audio: AAC, Dolby Digital 2ch 48kHz/16-bit, Linear PCM File: MP4, MOV, AVCHD Modes (59.94Hz) 150 Mbps (MOV/MP4): 4096×2160 (23.98p, 29.97p, 59.94p) 100 Mbps (MOV/MP4): 4096×2160 (23.98p, 29.97p) 150 Mbps (MOV/MP4): 3840×2160 (23.98p, 29.97p, 59,94p) 100 Mbps (MOV/MP4): 3840×2160 (23.98p, 29.97p) 200 Mbps (MOV/MP4): 1920×1080 (23.98p, 29.97p, 59.94p) 100 Mbps (MOV/MP4): 1920×1080 (23.98p, 29.97p, 59.94p) 72 Mbps (MP4 only): 1920×1080 (23.98p, 29.97p) 28 Mbps (MP4 only): 1920×1080 (59.94p) 24 Mbps (AVCHD/MP4): 1920×1080 (23.98p)  24 Mbps (AVCHD only): 1920×1080 (59.94i with 29.97fps sensor output) 20 Mbps (MP4 only): 1920×1080 (29.97) 17 Mbps (AVCHD only): 1920×1080 (59.94i with 59.94fps sensor output) Media Type: SD, SDHC, SDXCHigh Resolution Recording Class Requirements: SDXC UHS-I / UHS-II UHS Speed Class 3 (U3)  Approximate Record Times200 Mbps: 0.7 Min/GB150 Mbps: 0.87 Min/GB100 Mbps: 1.25 Min/GB Maximum Record TimeContinuousFiles may split after 96GB in some instancesMulti-Slot Recording Methods Dual Recording Relay Recording","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Swivel","Sensor Size":"Micro 4/3","Stabilization":"No","Viewfinder Type":"Electronic","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Wireless":"Wi-FiWi-Fi2.4GHz (STA/AP) (IEEE802.11b/g/n)Wi-Fi5GHz (STA) (IEEE 802.11a/n/ac)BluetoothBluetooth® v4.2 (Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE))","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Panasonic
