INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2560, 1, 183, 'Panasonic LUMIX BGH1 Cinema 4K', 'panasonic-lumix-bgh1-cinema-4k', 'The Panasonic LUMIX BGH1 Cinema 4K is a pro-grade box-style video camera for the Micro 4/3 system and even more video focused counterpart of the GH5S. Key features include:

10.2 MP, low-light optimized MOS sensor
Internal DCI 4K/60p with no sensor crop or time limit
Dual native ISO at ISO 400 & ISO 2500
Netflix approved camera

What’s In The Box? The GH5S was quite advanced for a hybrid photo/video mirrorless camera, and the Panasonic LUMIX BGH1 Cinema 4K does everything it did in a more compact, box-style camera housing that can be conveniently mounted on gimbals and hard to reach places. The BGH1 is not able to take still shots, and uses the video centric Panasonic VBR-series batteries for power as well as including an AC adapter. This camera also does not come with a display, so you’ll need a monitor. Several options are available under the “Accessories” tab on the left side of the screen.

10.28MP, Low-Light Optimized Sensor. The sensor is directly carried over from the GH5S with 10.28 megapixels Less and larger pixels take in more light and double its ISO sensitivity to 51,200. Dual native ISO of 400 & 2500 extends dynamic range in more shooting situations, especially when paired with the camera’s preinstalled V-Log L.

DCI 4K At 60 Frames Per Second. Options for DCI and UHD 4K are included here. The camera supports 4K/60p in 4:2:0 8-bit, but drop the frame rate to 30p for glorious 4K 4:2:2 10-bit at 400Mbps. High frame rate shooting is available at up to 240 fps in 1080p.

V-LogL Upgrade Installed. Panasonic did everyone a solid and decided to preinstall the V-Log L upgrade on all copies of this camera. This provides an extremely flat gamma curve and image that’s capable of 13-stops of dynamic range for additional latitude when grading your footage.

Timecode In/Out.  BNC Timecode and Genlock ports allow for professional time code and sync options without the need for adapters. RJ45 Gigabit LAN also allows for network syncing.

Need a Memory Card? You’ll need an ultra-fast memory card for a camera this powerful, and we recommend the Sony 128GB SF-G Tough Series UHS-II SDXC. This camera can take full advantage of its superior 299 MB/s max write speed and 300 MB/s max read speed for high-resolution, high-bitrate capture.', 411000.0, '{"Brand":"Panasonic","Camera Mount":"Micro 4/3","Camera Type":"Cinema","Compatible Media":"SD","Crop Factor":"2x","Imaging":"SensorType: Live MOSSize: 19 × 13mm (4/3\\")Effective Pixels10.2MPISODynamic Range: Up to 13 stopsDefault Sensitivity: 160 – 51,200Expanded Sensitivity: 80 – 204,800Base: 160 / 800","Inputs/Outputs":"Audio InputsMic In (3.5mm stereo mini jack)Audio OutputsHeadphones Out (3.5mm stereo mini jack)Video OutputsHDMI Type-A3G-SDI BNCAdditional Inputs/OutputsRemote: 2.5mm LANCTimecode In/Out: BNCGenlock In: BNC, BBS signal / tri-level syncLAN: RJ-45 / PoE+USB: 3.1 GEN1 Type-CDC In: 12V (11.4V to 12.6V)","Item Type":"Camera","Maximum Video Resolution":"4K","Memory Type":"(2) UHS-II SDXC","Physical":"Dimensions3.7 × 3.7 × 3.1″Weight1.2 lb","Sensor Size":"Micro 4/3","Stabilization":"No","Video Format":"Resolution @ framerate4096 × 2160p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97, 50, 59.94 fps3840 × 2160p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97, 50, 59.94 fps3680 X 2760p at 23.98, 25, 29.97, 50, 59.943328 × 2496p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97, 50, 59.94 fps1920 × 1080p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97, 50, 59.94 fpsCodecsAVC-Intra/AVC-LongG/H.264 Long GOP/H.265/MOV 4:2:0 10-BitAVC-Intra/AVC-LongG/H.264 Long GOP/H.265/MOV 4:2:0 8-BitAVC-Intra/AVC-LongG/H.264 Long GOP/H.265/MP4 4:2:0 10-BitAVC-Intra/AVC-LongG/H.264/H.264 Long GOP/H.265/MP4 4:2:0 8-BitHDMI Output12-bit RAW output over HDMI to Blackmagic Video Assist or Ninja V4","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Wireless Connectivity":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'LUMIX
