INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2789, 1, 202, 'Ricoh GR IV', 'ricoh-gr-iv', 'The Ricoh GR IV is a compact, fixed lens camera designed with major updates to the popular GR IIIx, including an upgraded sensor, increased built-in memory, and more. Key features include:

25.7MP APS-C BSI CMOS sensor
28mm lens with built-in ND filter
53GB of internal storage & microSD slot
Image stabilization & 1080p60 video

What’s Changed? Rolling off the back of the previous GR IIIx, this Ricoh GR IV comes equipped with several internal and external improvements. Its impressive 25.7MP BSI CMOS sensor and fixed 28mm-equivalent lens work in tandem with one another to produce exceptional quality photo and video, while improved autofocus and Shake Reduction help the camera keep up with fast, handheld shooting. Additionally, this camera is supported with increased built-in memory, an updated battery, and minor tweaks to focusing and shooting modes.

Upgraded Sensor and Processor. The GR IV’s sensor and sharp GR ENGINE 7 processor deliver optimal performance, even in low-light environments. Boasting a rapid 0.6-sec startup time and ISO up to 204800, your focusing needs are supported. Following suit with its predecessor, this camera also captures versatile 14-bit DNG and JPEG recording.

5-Axis Stabilization System. Compensating for up to 6 stops of camera shake, the GR IV’s improves on the 3-axis reduction of the GR IIIx with a more handheld-friendly 5-axis system.

Fixed Lens and Optical Design. Sporting an integrated wide-angle 28mm f/2.8-equivalent lens, the GR IV supports simple, everyday capture while giving you a leg up in low-light scenarios. Its upgraded optical design features a 7 element/5 group layout engineered with aspherical, HR, and low-dispersion glass elements, delivering clarity while maintaining a lightweight physical design. In Macro Mode, the GR IV boasts close focusing distances of 2.4-inches to 4.7-inches, while its integrated ND filter reduces exposure by 2-stops to maximize aperture settings or minimizing shutter speeds for cool effects. Additionally, built-in crop modes takes this camera a step further by simulating 35mm and 50mm field of views, eliminating the need for extra lenses.

Physical Design and Power. Keeping the light-yet-durable magnesium alloy blend of its predecessor, this camera features a slimmer design for a more secure handheld grip. With an uptick in storage capacity, the GR IV supports up to 53GB of internal memory, along with a microSD card slot. Along with this updated camera comes an updated battery, the DB-120. This larger-capacity battery captures up to 250 shots per charge compared to the 200 shots of the GR IIIx, while the integrated USB-C port allows for in-camera battery charging and data transfer.

Controls and Display. The updated control layout on the GR IV gives you easier access to immediate adjustments and provides a more intuitive, user-friendly experience. At the center of your controls, the 3-inch LCD touchscreen promotes increased visibility outdoors thanks to its air gapless design, and is even further supported when the Outdoor Monitor Setting function is engaged!

GR World App. Outside of your standard Bluetooth and Wi-Fi support, Ricoh’s GR World App further improves user experience by providing you with a home base for file transfer, remote shutter release, and location data transfer.

GR Accessories Available. Amp up your image capture with an array of GR-compatible accessories! Available separately, the GR IV accepts the GA-1 and GA-3 lens adapters, the GW-4 Wide Conversion Lens (when used with GA-3 adapter), and the GF-2 External Flash.', 336000.0, '{"Battery":"1x DB-120 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 3.85 VDC, 1800 mAh (Included)Approx. 250 Shots","Brand":"Ricoh","Camera Type":"Compact","Compatible Media":"microSD","Dimensions":"(W x H x D) 4.3 × 2.4 × 1.3″","Exposure Control":"Shutter SpeedMechanical Shutter: 1/4000 to 30 Seconds Bulb/Time ModeBulb & Time Mode (Up to 20 Minutes) ISO/Gain SensitivityNative: 100 to 204,800 Metering MethodCenter-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, Multi, Spot Exposure ModesAperture Priority, Auto, Program, Shutter Priority Exposure Compensation -5 to +5 EV (1/3 EV Steps) White Balance Presets AutoCTECloudyColor Temperature DaylightFluorescent (Cool White)Fluorescent (Daylight)Fluorescent (Warm White)ShadeTungsten Interval RecordingYes Self-Timer2/10-Second Delay","Flash":"Built-In Flash/LightNo External Flash ConnectionShoe Mount","Imaging":"Sensor ResolutionEffective: 25.74 Megapixel (6192 × 4128) Image Sensor23.3 × 15.5 mm (APS-C) CMOS","Interface":"Internal Storage53 GB Video I/ONo Audio I/ONo Power I/O1x USB-C Input Other I/O1x USB-C Data Output (Shared with Power Input) Mobile App CompatibleYes: Android & iOSApp Name: GR WORLD Global Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)No","Item Type":"Camera","Lens":"Focal Length18.3mm (35mm Equivalent: 28mm) Digital Zoom1.8x Maximum ApertureMaximum: f/2.8Minimum: f/16 Focus RangeNormal: 3.9\\" to Infinity / 10 cm to InfinityMacro: 2.4\\" to 5.9\\" / 6 cm to 15 cm Optical Design7 Elements in 5 Groups","Maximum Video Resolution":"1080p","Mfr. Model Number":"#01553","Physical":"Environmental ResistanceNo Shoe Mount1x Hot Shoe","Screen Resolution":"1,037,000 Dot","Screen Type":"Touchscreen and Fixed","Sensor Size":"APS-C","Stabilization":"Yes","Still Image Capture":"Aspect Ratio1:1,