	Sony NEX-VG30', 29000.0, '{"Brand":"Sanho","Cable Type":"Video","Connector":"HDMI and Mini HDMI","Item Type":"Cable","Length":"2.6’"}', 'Just the cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2951, 4, 208, 'Sanho 2.6ft HyperThin HDMI Micro-Mini', 'sanho-2-6ft-hyperthin-hdmi-micro-mini', 'The Sanho 2.6ft HyperThin HDMI Micro-Mini is an ultra-thin cable with Micro-HDMI male (type-D) to Mini-HDMI (type C) connector. Key features include:

4K capable
Ultra-thin short-run cable
Excellent for gimbal systems
Micro-Mini HDMI cable

4K Capable. This HDMI v1.4 cable supports Full HD 1080p all the way up 8K resolution, with 15.8 Gbps data throughput that transmits 7.1-channel digital surround audio, 240Hz video image refresh, and 48-bit color. If you’re looking for a cable to record 4K from the Sony a7s to an external recorder, you’ve come to the right place. In fact, this is the only place!

Short Run. When you need to cover a short distance and don’t want to deal with excess cable, the Sanho 2.6ft HyperThin HDMI Micro-Mini is a great option for your HDMI needs. While they’re perfectly suitable for cameras and monitors, these cables work great with our gimbal systems. We strongly recommend them as viable options for Ronins and Movis due to their light weight, ideal length, and dependability.

Please Note: This is not your standard, run-of-the-mill HDMI cable. It’s quite difficult to find a cable that goes from micro-HDMI (type D) to mini-HDMI (type C), particularly one that transmits 4K. Unless you’ve been searching for a cable for external 4K recording from the a7S to Odyssey7Q+, chances are this isn’t the correct cable for you.', 25000.0, '{"Brand":"Sanho","Cable Type":"Video","Connector":"Mini HDMI and Micro HDMI","Item Type":"Cable","Length":"2.6’"}', 'Just the cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2952, 5, 209, 'Schneider 4 x 5.65" True-Streak Confetti Filter', 'schneider-4-x-5-65-true-streak-confetti-filter', 'Capture any bright light source within your image while using the Schneider 4 × 5.65″ True-Streak Confetti Filter and see an explosion of color. The True-Streak Confetti Filter is an unusual specialty filter that produces flares of multi-colored streaks of varying size and length that emanate from bright points of light in photo and video images.', 125000.0, '{"Brand":"Schneider","Filter Format":"4×5.6","Filter Type":"Flare Effect","Item Type":"Lens Support","Lens Support Type":"Filter","Mfr. Model Number":"68-515056"}', 'Schneider 4 × 5.65″
True-Streak
Confetti
Filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2953, 5, 209, 'Schneider 4 x 5.65" True-Streak Rainbow Filter', 'schneider-4-x-5-65-true-streak-rainbow-filter', 'The Schneider 4 × 5.65″ Rainbow True-Streak Filter creates prominent, elongated streaks that are symmetric and extend horizontally from point light sources within a scene. Key features include:

Streak effect from point light source
Horizontal streaks from light source
Spectrum of up to 7 colors for streaks
Anamorphic, symmetric, and elongated streaks

Streaks & Lighting. The Schneider 4 × 4″ Rainbow True-Streak Filter is designed to be used at a 90° angle to a point-light source such as the sun, a light bulb, or a candle. This filter creates streaks extending from point-light sources which each assume the characteristics of a continuous spectrum. With a spectrum of up to seven streak colors (red, orange, yellow, green, blue, pink, and violet), shorter streaks are proportionate to less prominent sources of illumination and may display a more limited number of colors which are determined by their relative position within the frame. The materials used to create optical clarity and color fidelity are constructed from water white glass, and is most effective for pictures where the light source used to generate the streak effect is a highlight with a significant degree of contrast from the rest of the image.

Anamorphic Projection. This filter allows the effect of anamorphic optics upon highlights to be reproduced when using optics that do not have an anamorphic design, and if an image or footage is captured with an anamorphic lens for the primary purpose of obtaining a greater aspect ratio than what is possible when only using spherical lenses on a 35mm format, the direct result will appear compressed and distorted. Projecting this compressed and distorted footage or imagery through a reverse anamorphic projection lens allows elements within the scene to be viewed in their correct proportions. A complementary effect of this process after it is completed is the creation of elongated, blue-colored, horizontally symmetrical highlights from point light sources that can extend through the frame.', 118000.0, '{"Brand":"Schneider","Filter Format":"4×5.6","Filter Type":"Flare Effect","Item Type":"Lens Support","Lens Support Type":"Filter"}', 'Schneider 4 × 5.65″
True-Streak
Rainbow
Filter
Filter pouch', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2954, 2, 209, 'Schneider Cine-Xenar III 18mm T2.2 EF', 'schneider-cine-xenar-iii-18mm-t2-2-ef', 'The Schneider Cine-Xenar III 18mm T2.2 EF is a high-quality Canon EF-mount cinema lens for use with Super35 sensor cameras. Key features include:

27mm-equivalent focal length after sensor-crop factor
Telecentric optical design for digital sensors
Extremely smooth and round bokeh
104mm outside diameter, 100mm x 0.75 filter thread

Super35 Coverage. The Schneider Cine-Xenar III 18mm T2.2 easily covers a Super35 film frame with 31.5mm image circle, providing support up to 2K/4K/5K Cinema.

Wide Angle. This lens provides a focal length equivalent to about 27mm after sensor-crop factor.

Cinema Lens Build. Across the board, the Cine-Xenar III lineup has an outside diameter of 104mm with a 100mm x 0.75 filter thread, and they’re all color-matched to allow simple lens changes. There’s virtually no breathing/change in image size when focusing and all focus and iris gears are in the same position.

High-Quality Optics. The telecentric optical design provides even sensor illumination, and the special Schneider-Kreuznach high-performance coating improves image performance and flare suppression. The eighteen-blade iris provides extremely smooth and round bokeh for exceptional backgrounds.', 589000.0, '{"Angle of View":"63.2º","Aperture Blades":"18","Brand":"Schneider","Dimensions":"4.1 × 7.1″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"100.0mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On and Matte Box Mount","Focal Length":"18-18","Focus Rotation":"270º","Focus Type":"Manual Focus Only","Front Lens Diameter":"104mm","Gearing":"0.8 MOD focus, iris","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Super35 and APS-C","Lens Mount":"Canon EF","Lens Type":"Wide Angle, Cine, and For DSLR","Maximum Aperture":"2.2","Mfr. Model Number":"1072700","Minimum Focusing Distance":"11\\"","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"No","Weight":"4.5 lb.","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Schneider
