Sigma I Series. The Sigma 24mm f/2 DG C belong’s to Sigma’s 1 Series group of lenses, which is a collection that prioritizes compactness without sacrificing performance. These lenses offer all-metal construction with precision-cut aluminum, an elegant finish, and pleasingly tactile knurled focus and aperture rings.

Stepping Motor. Equipped with a stepping AF motor, this lens has admirable autofocus speeds for videography. This is complemented by a manual aperture ring and an AF/MF toggle with a raised arc shape for fast switching. Please note that the aperture ring is not de-clickable and has 1/3-stop clicks.

Wide Field of View. This lens captures a sense of space without the distortion and has a close focusing distance of under 10" for beautiful closeups that still include the surrounding environment. With an f/2 maximum aperture, this lens is suitable for low-light subjects and is a great option for landscapes, cityscapes, and nightscapes.

Try it with These E-Mount Cameras. The portable nature of this lens makes it a great option for shooters on the go and pairs well with slightly more compact cameras like the Sony ZV-E1 or the Sony Alpha a7C II. However, it’ll work with any E-mount system, including APS-C sensor cameras like the Sony a6600, where it will provide an equivalent focal length of 36mm.', 182000.0, '{"Angle of View":"84.1°","Aperture Blades":"9, rounded","Brand":"Sigma","Dimensions":"2.8 × 2.9″ (ø x L)","Filter Size":"62.0mm","Filter Type":"Screw-On","Focal Length":"24-24","Focus Type":"Autofocus","Groups/Elements":"11/13","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Format":"Full-Frame","Lens Mount":"Sony E","Lens Type":"Wide Angle and For Mirrorless","Maximum Aperture":"2.0","Maximum Magnification":"0.15x","Mfr. Model Number":"4B3965","Minimum Focusing Distance":"9.6\\"","Stabilization":"No","Weather Sealing":"Yes","Weight":"0.79 lb.","Zoom Type":"Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Sigma 24mm f/2
