What’s Changed? Unlike its predecessor, the Sigma Cine 105mm T1.5 FF Prime with /i Technology supports Cooke’s /i metadata protocols to communicate with the camera, recording optical characteristics and lens settings to every frame to make post-production easier. This is especially useful when you’re adding effects in post.

Mid-Range Prime. This lens offers full-frame coverage, giving you a compact, lightweight, mid-range cine lens. It’s capable of delivering 6K to 8K resolution, and its fast T1.5 aperture allows depth-of-field control and low-light shooting flexibility.

