INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (3216, 2, 214, 'Sigma Cine 135mm T2.0 FF Prime w/ i Technology (PL)', 'sigma-cine-135mm-t2-0-ff-prime-w-i-technology-pl', 'The enhanced Sigma Cine 135mm T2.0 FF Prime w/ i Technology combines the same high-quality optics and mechanics of its FF prime line with a cine-oriented design, and it now utilizes Cooke /i Technology that provides lens metadata. Key features include:

Covers Full-Frame sensor sizes
Supports Cooke /i metadata technology
Stepless, 0.8 pitch gear aperture and focus rings
Standardized focus and iris gear ring positions

PL Mount. We carry this lens in several different mounts. This is the PL-mount version.

Cooke/i Technology. By using an /i Technology-compatible cine lens with a cine camera that supports the same protocol, users can see and record lens metadata such as focus distance, focal length, and aperture. This helps streamline compositing in the post production process. This is particularly suitable for the latest forms of filmmaking, such as VFX, that call for detailed shooting data. Prototypes of these /i Technology-compatible FF High Speed Prime lens were used for shooting 2021’s Top Gun Maverick, proving that the new lenses are already in commercial applications.

Telephoto Prime. The Sigma Cine 135mm T2.0 offers full-frame coverage, giving you a compact, lightweight, wide-angle cine lens. It’s capable of delivering 6K to 8K resolution, and its fast T2.0 aperture allows depth-of-field control and low-light shooting flexibility.

High-Quality Optics. This lens’s optics are designed to minimize flare and ghosting while enhancing contrast, even in backlit conditions. You’ll get exceptional bokeh, and maximum sharpness across the frame.

