INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (3376, 1, 219, 'Sony Alpha a1 II', 'sony-alpha-a1-ii', 'The Sony Alpha a1 II is a full-frame, high-resolution mirrorless camera designed around the previous Sony a1, with updates such as an AI processing unit, pre-capture and speed boost functions, and more. Key features include:

50MP full-frame stacked BSI CMOS sensor
Up to 30 fps shooting with AF/AE
4-axis touchscreen LCD
Dual CFexpress Type A/SD card slots

What’s Changed? The Sony Alpha a1 II brings you the versatility of the Sony a1 with updated features, including an AI processing unit that pushes the boundaries of autofocus, subject detection, and subject tracking capabilities. This processing unit enables the camera to accurately recognize and intelligently predict the movements of your subject, all while retaining clear focus. For those intense movement shots during sports and wildlife action, Pre-Capture and Speed Boost functions are committed to delivering continuous burst-style shooting, allowing you to capture every moment. Additionally, the a1 II boasts a refined 5-axis 8.5-stop in-body image stabilization (IBIS), stacking an extra 3 stops to the performance of its predecessor. This feature builds on the already existing versatility of the a1 series, and allows you to shoot handheld in dimmer lighting conditions with slower shutter speeds.

8K 30p Video Capture and More. With familiar 8K 30p with 10-bit 4:2:0 sampling and 4K 120p with 10-bit 4:2:2 sampling, the a1 II uses its upgraded BIONZ XR processing and previously mentioned features to improve imaging performance and shooting rates. This camera is capable of up to 30 fps continuous shooting with an electronic shutter, or 10 fps with the mechanical shutter, with AF and AE supported. It retains the same full-frame 50MP BSI CMOS sensor as its predecessor, delivering a fusion of high-resolution imagery with the speed and reduced rolling shutter of a stacked design.

QXGA OLED EVF and Vari-Angle Touchscreen LCD. The QXGA OLED Tru-Finder EVF boasts a high 9.44m-dot resolution and 0.9x magnification for bright, sharp eye-level viewing. Its 240 fps High Quality+ setting gives you smooth motion rendering. The side-opening, 3.2-inch, 2.1m-dot touchscreen LCD is great for easy, intuitive menu navigation and shooting control, and its articulating design lets you work from a range of angles.

Ports, Memory, N’ Power. You’ve got everything you need for transferring and monitoring right on the side of the a1 II: a USB-C port with fast USB 3.2 Gen 2 speeds of up to 10 Gb/s, a full-size HDMI port, an upgraded 2.5GBASE-T wired LAN port, a sync port, and a RJ45 port. Of course, you’ll have your basic micro-USB and 3.5mm audio monitoring/microphone ports as well! To prevent accidental cable disconnections, we have the Sony Alpha A1 II Cable Protector. Like previous Alpha models, the a1 II is fueled via a single included Sony NP-FZ100 Battery.

Other Notable Features. The a1 II’s updated menu structure is a welcome change from those found in previous Alpha-series cameras, and you can navigate the menus via the touchscreen much like you can on the a7S III. There are hot-shoe and PC-terminal external-flash connections, automatic anti-flicker shutter timing, built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth capabilities for wireless image sharing and camera control, and NFC for one-touch connection between the a1 II and compatible mobile devices. The dual memory-card slots both accept CFexpress Type A and SD memory cards, and the camera uses the rechargeable NP-FZ100 battery that’s rated for 420 shots/90 minutes of recording per charge.', 1350000.0, '{"Brand":"Sony","Camera Mount":"Sony E","Camera Type":"Mirrorless","Compatible Media":"CFexpress Type A and SD","Exposure Control":"Shutter TypeMechanical Focal Plane Shutter and Electronic Rolling Shutter Shutter SpeedMechanical Shutter: 1/8000 to 30 SecondsElectronic Shutter:1/32000 to 30 Seconds, 1/8000 to 1/4 Second in Movie Mode Bulb/Time ModeBulb Mode Metering MethodAverage, Center-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, Multi, Spot Exposure ModesAperture Priority, Auto, Manual, Program, Shutter Priority Exposure Compensation -5 to +5 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps) Metering Range -3 to 20 EV White Balance2500 to 9900KPresets: Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Custom, Daylight, Flash, Fluorescent (Cool White), Fluorescent (Day White), Fluorescent (Daylight), Fluorescent (Warm White), Incandescent, Shade, Underwater Continuous ShootingUp to 30 fps at Maximum Resolution for up to 240 Frames (Raw) / 400 Frames (JPEG) Interval RecordingYes Self-Timer2/5/10-Second Delay","External Video Recording Modes":"4:2:0 8-Bit via HDMIUHD 8K (7680 × 4320) at 23.98/25/29.97 fpsUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.98/29.97/59.94 fps1920 × 1080p at 23.98/29.97/50/59.94 fps1920 × 1080i at 50/59.94 fps 4:2:2 10-Bit via HDMIUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps1920 × 1080p at 23.98/29.97/50/59.94 fps1920 × 1080i at 50/59.94 fps Raw 16-Bit via HDMI4332 × 2446 at 23.98/29.97/59.94 fps","Flash":"Built-In Flash/LightNo Flash ModesAuto, Fill Flash, Hi-Speed Sync, Off, Rear Sync, Red-Eye Reduction, Slow Sync Maximum Sync Speed1/400 Second Flash Compensation -3 to +3 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps) Dedicated Flash SystemTTL External Flash ConnectionShoe Mount, PC Terminal","Focus":"Focus TypeAuto and Manual Focus Focus ModeContinuous-Servo AF, Direct Manual Focus, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AF Autofocus Points Phase Detection: 759 Autofocus Sensitivity -4 to +20 EV","General":"Battery Type1x NP-FZ100 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7.2 VDC, 2280 mAh (Approx. 420 Shots) Shoe Mount1x Intelligent Hot Shoe Tripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom) Material of ConstructionMagnesium Alloy Operating Conditions32 to 104°F Dimensions (W x H x D)5.4 × 3.8 × 3.3″  Weight23.2 oz26.2 oz (With Battery, Recording Media)","ISO Sensitivity Range":"Photo100 to 32,000 in Manual Mode (Extended: 50 to 102,400)100 to 12,800 in Auto Mode Video100 to 32,000 in Manual Mode100 to 12,800 in Auto Mode","Imaging":"Lens MountSony E Sensor ResolutionActual: 50.5 MegapixelEffective: 50.1 Megapixel (8640 × 5760) Image Sensor35.9 × 24 mm (Full-Frame) Stacked CMOS Sensor Crop (35mm Equivalent)Crop Factor: 1xAdditional Modes: 1.5x\\n *Additional Crop Occurs in Select Video Modes Image StabilizationSensor-Shift, 5-Axis Built-In ND FilterNo Capture TypeStills & Video","Interface":"Media/Memory Card SlotDual Slot: CFexpress Type A / SD (UHS-II) Video I/O1x HDMI Output Audio I/O\\t1x 1/8\\" / 3.5 mm TRS Stereo Headphone Output1x 1/8\\" / 3.5 mm TRS Stereo Microphone Input Power I/O1x USB-C Input Other I/O1x RJ45 Data Output1x USB-C (USB 3.2 / 3.1 Gen 2) Data/Remote Input/Output (Shared with Power Input)1x PC Flash Sync Output1x Sony Multi/Micro-USB Remote/Time Code Input Wireless2.4 / 5 GHz Wi-Fi 5 (802.11ac), Bluetooth 5.0 Mobile App CompatibleYes: Android & iOSApp Name: Creators’ AppFunctionality: Access Stored Files,