INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (3555, 1, 219, 'Sony PXW-FS7M2 4K Premium Kit', 'sony-pxw-fs7m2-4k-premium-kit', 'We built the Sony PXW-FS7M2 4K Premium Kit for renters who want a pick-up-and-shoot 4K rig, but want the flexibility to choose their own lenses. See the Includes section to the right for a full item listing. Key features of the FS7M2 include:

Reinforced Locking E-Mount
Electronic Variable ND
Netflix approved camera
BT. 2020 HDR Image Support

What’s Different? Since the FS7M2 is not a replacement for the FS7, the most important question is not what’s new, but instead what makes it different from the original. The biggest improvements include a brand new, first-of-its-kind locking E-Mount, Electronic Variable ND (as seen on the FS5), and general improvements to the construction and user experience.

Reinforced Locking E-Mount. Now instead of docking and twisting, just insert the lens without rotating and turn the locking ring. The new locking E-Mount is a part of a brand new reinforced camera front that has better support for cine lenses.

Electronic Variable ND. The Electronic Variable ND works in one of three different ways. The first is like a conventional ND filter wheel, with 4 set positions you can swap between. Second, you can rotate the knob and ease through seven stops of filtration like a lens front mounted variable ND. Lastly, the FS7 Mark II’s auto ND function allows you to lock your shutter speed and aperture despite changing lighting environments.

Refined Build Quality. The FS7 II features a tool-less design, meaning you can make adjustments to the Smart Grip or the viewfinder on the fly without having to pull out a screwdriver. The number of user programmable buttons has increased from 6 to 10, giving operators a greater level of control.

High Dynamic Range. The FS7M II uses the same super35 as the original model, which means 14 stops of dynamic range. The big upgrade in the II is the addition of the REC BT.2020 color space with full support HDR imagery.', 1079000.0, '{"Brand":"Sony","Camera Mount":"Sony E","Camera Type":"Cinema","Item Type":"Camera"}', 'Sony
