INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (3685, 2, 227, 'Tamron 28-75mm f/2.8 Di III VXD G2 for Nikon Z', 'tamron-28-75mm-f-2-8-di-iii-vxd-g2-for-nikon-z', 'The Tamron 28-75mm f/2.8 Di III VXD G2 is a full-frame, Nikon Z-mount zoom offering a versatile wide-to-portrait-length range. Key features include:

Voice-coil eXtreme-torque Drive linear AF motor
Bright constant f/2.8 maximum aperture
Updated ergonomic design
Ideal for travel, candids, events, and portraits

Compact Ultra-Telephoto Zoom. Covering a wide to portrait-length range, the Tamron 28-75mm f/2.8 Di III VXD G2 for Nikon Z is a versatile lens that is remarkably portable: only 4.7" long and under 2 lb. With one lens you can cover portraits, street photography, travel, and events. On a crop-sensor camera this lens will provide an equivalent 42-112.5mm range.

Enhanced Form Factor and Operation. Tamron made some key structural tweaks to this lens for a user-friendly experience. The arc rotation of the zoom ring has been shortened so that you can reach your desired focal length quickly. The rubber on the ring has also been improved for better grip with deeper grooves. A curvier, more contoured profile makes the entire lens more ergonomic and comfortable to hold and the focus setting buttons on the barrel are surrounded by a bevel that naturally guides your finger to position. All of this, along with its overall compactness, allows this lens to be used all day without fatigue.

Outstanding Performance in Various Conditions. The Tamron 28-75mm f/2.8 Di III VXD G2 for Nikon Z is equipped with a Voice-coil eXtreme-torque Drive (VXD) linear motor focus mechanism for advanced autofocusing with excellent tracking performance in low light. Close focusing has been improved over the prior version and the optical system has been redesigned for edge-to-edge sharpness.

Try it with These Z-Mount Cameras. The portable nature of this lens makes it a great option for shooters on the go and pairs well with slightly more compact cameras like the Nikon Z8. It’s also a great all-in-one lens that you can use all day and is a suitable companion to a long-lasting camera such as the Nikon Z9, which boasts a 750-shot-per-charge lifespan, a durable build, and thoughtful ergonomics.', 211000.0, '{"Brand":"Tamron","Item Type":"Lens","Lens Mount":"Nikon Z","Lens Type":"Wide Angle and Standard","Optical Design":"Groups/Elements15/17Aperture Blades9, Rounded"}', 'Tamron 28-75mm f/2.8
