INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (3863, 5, 233, 'Tilta Nucleus Nano II FIZ Lens Control Motor', 'tilta-nucleus-nano-ii-fiz-lens-control-motor', 'The Tilta Nucleus Nano II FIZ Lens Control Motor powers the focus, iris, and zoom functions of your FIZ system. Key features include:

15mm single-rod clamp
LED indicator & pairing button
0.8 MOD gearing
Automatic or manual lens calibration

FIZ Functional. The Tilta Nucleus Nano II FIZ Lens Control Motor connects easily to your rig using the 15mm single-rod clamp, and offers an increased torque for efficient moves. Designed to power the focus, iris and zoom functions of your FIZ system, this unit is positioned offset from the main gearing, which helps keep everything in place and prevents the motor from pushing away from the lens. This motor has a 0.8 MOD, making it compatible with a variety of cinema-standard lenses.

Ports and Connectivity. The Nano II provides two USB-C ports, one as an input/output, and one as input only. These ports can power the motor and pass-through power to multiple motors to control FIZ from one individual source. As for connectivity, this motor provides built-in  2.4 GHz Wi-Fi that enables you to connect to the separately available Nano II Handwheel.

LED Guide. Once connected to your rig, you’ll notice an LED indicator lights up. A green light indicates iris control, a blue light indicates zoom control, and a purple light indicates focus control. If you see a yellow light pop up, fret not, it means literally nothing. Think of it as a “you’re doing a good job” indicator.', 79000.0, '{"Brand":"Tilta","Gear Mod":"0.8 MOD","Inputs/Outputs":"1 x USB-C I/O 1 x USB-C Input","Item Type":"Lens Support","LED Indicators":"GreenIris control BlueZoom control PurpleFocus control YellowUnassigned","Lens Support Type":"Lens Control","Wireless":"2.4 GHz Wi-Fi"}', 'Tilta
Nucleus
Nano
